Created On    : 31-Oct-2008 / alvi
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : SETUP009: added jpaconsole
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : you can now run jpa-ql queries in realtime without deploying
        the application. Here's how it works:

        first, run:
                 adnant jpaconsole

             the tool will now run and display sth like this:

             [java] 19:16:04,588 INFO  [                 Gdi:335 ] generated 2 files in '/tmp/jpaconsole'
             [java] 19:16:04,589 INFO  [    TemplateDesigner:234 ]
             [java] 19:16:04,590 INFO  [    TemplateDesigner:235 ] template: /local/alvi/projects/logon/etc/gdi/jpaconsole/cartridge/templates/createNativeQuery4all.vm
             [java] 19:16:04,590 INFO  [    TemplateDesigner:236 ]  example: /tmp/jpaconsole/createNativeQuery4all.vm
             [java] 19:16:04,590 INFO  [    TemplateDesigner:234 ]
             [java] 19:16:04,590 INFO  [    TemplateDesigner:235 ] template: /local/alvi/projects/logon/etc/gdi/jpaconsole/cartridge/templates/createQuery4all.vm
             [java] 19:16:04,591 INFO  [    TemplateDesigner:236 ]  example: /tmp/jpaconsole/createQuery4all.vm

        Note that the tool will not exit, it will look for changes and rerun your jpa-ql query.

        Now, open this file in an editor:

             /local/alvi/projects/logon/etc/gdi/jpaconsole/cartridge/templates/createQuery4all.vm

         ... and in the shell, start this:

            xterm -e watch -n0 cat /tmp/jpaconsole/createQuery4all.vm

        The first file is the template in which you can define your query:

           #set ($query = "select cat.name, dog.name from Cat cat, Dog dog")

        The second file (in /tmp/jpaconsole) will contain the result of
        the query after you've saved the template file:

        +----------------------+--------------+
        |fermat, the clever cat|          lupo|
        |               nibbles|          lupo|
        |                 snuki|          lupo|
        |fermat, the clever cat|bosco, the dog|
        |               nibbles|bosco, the dog|
        |                 snuki|bosco, the dog|
        +----------------------+--------------+

        Whenever you change the query and save the file, the result file
        '/tmp/jpaconsole/createQuery4all.vm' will be refreshed automatically.

        In the tool's output log, you will see the sql that is being sent to the DB, e.g.:

             [java] Hibernate:
             [java]     select
             [java]         cat0_.NAME as col_0_0_,
             [java]         dog1_.name as col_1_0_
             [java]     from
             [java]         CAT cat0_,
             [java]         DOG dog1_
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M build-test.xml
A etc/gdi/jpaconsole/cartridge/README
A etc/gdi/jpaconsole/cartridge/toolbox.xml
A etc/gdi/jpaconsole/cartridge/templates/createNativeQuery4all.vm
A etc/gdi/jpaconsole/cartridge/templates/createQuery4all.vm
A etc/gdi/jpaconsole/test/result.properties
