Created On    : 16-Dec-2008 / istvan
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS032: call flush() on every write operation in the entity manager
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : 
       - exceptions in the business didn't contain the business method
       - deletion and inserts lead to 'java.sql.BatchUpdateException: ORA-00001: unique constraint (ULGN01.UQ_TLGNU_USER_BILLTO_BP_ACC) violated'
Description   : 
       - we now call 'flush()' whenever we change data. see (from (http://www.oracle.com/technology/tech/java/oc4j/ejb3/how_to/howtoejb30entitymanager/doc/how-to-ejb30-entitymanager.html#flush)):

            EntityManager flush()

The EntityManager flush() API is used to send updates to the database within a transaction, subsequent queries within the same transaction will return the updated data. This is usefull if a particular transaction spans mutiple operations or pages, similar to a "wizard".

       -> this way we ensure that the code is always consistent with the 'perceived' changes on the DB.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/persistence/DaoSupport.java

