Created On    : 12-Jan-2009 / alvi
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : CFG017: fixed target/dist structure, using java5 jdbc driver (for easy switch back to java 5)
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : 
		- using java5 jdbc driver for now. I suspect that sone of the 'cant overwrite cause'-exceptions 
		  come from non-j5/j6-ready libraries
		- the target/dist looks like this:
		      - etc/
		          log4j.xml - an external log4j.xml in case the default trace-settings need to be overriden
		          logon.properties - an external file which contains properties neccessary for the ap to work
		      - lib/
		          logon-app.ear - ear to deploy
		- Notes:
		      - the location of the logon.properties file must be determined at build time in
		        config/build.properties (config/build-local_tmpl.properties respectively)
		      - this path ends up in the file 
		           ./logon-common-web/target/generated/gdi/properties/spring_configurationContext.xml
		      - properties will come from the DB in a future release, this is a temporary solution
		      - log4j.xml can be used by way of setting the system property 'external_log4j_config'
		        within the container. This is optional, if omitted, the log4j.xml contained within
		        the ear will be used.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M build.xml
M properties.xml
M config/build.properties
M config/env.proj
M logon-business/properties.xml
M config/build-local_tmpl.properties
M logon-common-web/build.xml
M logon-common-web/etc/gdi/properties/templates/spring_configurationContext_4all.xml.vm
M logon-persistence/properties.xml

