Created On    : 16-Feb-2009 / zsolt
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : SAPSERVICE060: writing defective SOAP-requests to files at server-side
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : - name of log-files: SoapRequest_<timestamp>.log, 
		where <timestamp> refers to the time in milliseconds, 
		when the defective request has been processed.
		- 2 new properties are entered into run.conf to determine,
		if these logfiles are requeired.
		log.soap.requests -> if true, defective requests are written to separate log files
		log.soap.requests.dir -> folder for the above mentioned log-files 
		(it must exist and it has to be "writeable" by the server-process!)
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
