Created On    : 20-Feb-2009 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : 39578
ADN Change ID : PERSIST213: Create Order: When quantity > 1 create sometimes several orders, depending on UOM
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : When user orders 3 trucks 27T, an order will be created
		with quantity=3 and UOM of 27 tons (each truck). Problem:
        An order for bulk must not consist of more than 1 truck (because disposition cannot handle this).
Description   : -
Fix           : tlgnr_uom_bs was extended by a flag CREATE_MULTI_ORDER_FLAG.
		It's logic is: "When creating an order and this flag is set,
		several orders will be created, depending on the order quantity.
		Example: 3 trucks will create 3 orders (true), but 2 BAGS or 4 TONS
		will still lead to only one order (false)"
        All UOM of type "truck" have this Flag set (changed DBs already, and refdata loader).
		Only DB changes done, not yet the logic behind this.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/etc/sql/refdata/tlgnr_uom.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgnr_uom_bs.xml

