---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Created On    : 26-Mar-2009 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : PERSIST333: fixed number type mapping in views from number/Double to number(p)/BigDecimal
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : adnant oraviews creates type "Double" for columns which are
	expected to be integers (BigDecimal), and thus breaks the build.
Description   : This happens in these two cases so far:
	- accessing a sys table, where the data type is "number" (no precision)
	- using nvl() function, where Oracle assumes "number" (although both
	  values are actually number(10).
Fix           : Use explicit cast( ... as number(10)) etc in the view
	definitions, to force a smaller (integer) type. GDI will then
	correctly identify the type and generate the expected BigDecimal/
	number(p) datatype.
	Similar problems are expected with "union", where Oracle may also
	use wider types than we want.
	The other fixes are missing mapping files, or minor changes in
	the type.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/database/views/vlgnc_dispo_order_list.xml
M logon-persistence/etc/database/views/vlgnr_mop_status.xml
A logon-persistence/etc/database/views/vlgnr_silo_type.xml
