Created On    : 03-Apr-2009 / zweifel
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : SETUP068: Enabling security modules for Dev and Pkg setups
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : With this change, security modules will be enabled in both Dev and Pkg setups

		Dev Setup (with LogonDevUsersRolesLoginModule):
		- Idea: Similar login to externalLogin at Holcim, dev user is 'logonadmin'
		- DB: The user 'logonadmin' should already be present in your DB, extLoginActiveFlag should be set
		- Procedure for the user: BasicAuth with a popup as-is
		- Procedure in the background: Check of the extLogin with Password, setting principal to userid and setting roles/functions from db

		Pkg Setup (with LogonLanUsersRolesLoginModule):
		- Idea: Automagically login with KerberosPrincipal, but using userid and roles/functions from db
		- DB: Your kerberos user must be in your DB with the correct ldap_holspace name
		- Procedure for the user: None, IE takes care of it
		- Procedure in the background: Check of kerberos user, setting principal to userid and setting roles/functions from db

		Please note:
		- logon.domain has been split to logon.domain.lan and logon.domain.dmz for the introduction of the dmz pkg
		- security for logon-init has been disabled as it must be accessible in the background for both lan and dmz

Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
