Created On    : 06-Apr-2009 / gabor
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS074, PERSIST360: Technical fields; refactoring, DAOs to logon-persistence
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : #1: DAO generation is moved to logon-persistence module now.
				There are 2 jars created in logon-persistence, a full,
				containing all classes (data access, used by logon-business),
				and another one used by clients only (entities, DTOs).

				#2: Technical fields are generated as additional fields
				in the tables (views are skipped) by the "mergexml"
				cartridge. Default values are introduced for the not-nullable
				columns as follows:
					- CTL_CRE_TS -> SYSTIMESTAMP
					- CTL_CRE_UID -> 0 ("system" user, non-enforced FK)
					- CTL_CNT -> 0
				When inserting/updating records through entities, the technical
				fields will be overwritten automatically, even if they are set by
				the user through the public setters (Q: are they necessary?).
				Open issue: update technical fields also when working in
				TableBrowser.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
