ADN Change ID : BUSINESS076, PERSIST369: Sorting in RefData tables
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Added methods for retrieval of sorted reference data.
                By default (or passing null as ordering property),
                all finders will order the results by the
                "txt" property, however, this is not a preferred way of
                using the feature. Please try to always tell, by which
                field you want to order.

				Hint #1: pass the ATTR_... constants to the refdata service
				as ordering property. If you want to refer a field in the
				primary key class you can do that as well (as soon as ATTR_...
				constants are generated for the PK fields).

				Hint #2: access refDataService directly from the web tier
				and don't create your own finder methods in other services.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
