Created On    : 20-Apr-2009 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 39019
ADN Change ID : PERSIST400, ORDER195, ADMIN319: Removing poolName usage added tag to replace it temporary(?)
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : From now there is no such as poolName in PoolEntity (TLGNC_POOL), it is stored in TLGNC_POOL_TX table, because it is
		language dependent from now, though it is not real refdata, so it is not included in refDataService.
		<holcim-common:poolNameTag objectName='entry'/> knows how to resolve the pool's name in case entry is a PoolEntity
		or several other type, see the simple PoolNameTag class if you want to use it. The tag is added to lay 
		out the pool's name according to the given locale, with the least change to code.
		In the followings you can use PoolAdminServiceBean's fetchPoolTxEntity if you need only the id, and the language 
		dependent name of the pool (for example for comboboxes). (with poolTxPK.poolId you can get poolId, and with name attribute 
		the name of the pool).
		If you need the full list of pools with the names with given locale there is fetchPoolTxEntities in PoolAdminServiceBean.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
