Test Ref      : -
Documentation : -
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Created On    : 28-Apr-2009 / alvi
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS094: dispatcher swallowed root cause of problems
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : 
		Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2009 13:19:57 +0200
		From: Alvaro Fussen <alvi@adnovum.hu>
		To: Emoke Bardoczy <Emoke.Bardoczy@adnovum.hu>, 
		 Cosmin Moldovan <cosmin.moldovan@adnovum.ch>,
		 Valdas Jasaitis <valdas.jasaitis@adnovum.hu>
		Subject: Re: loggggggggggggggggg tons
		
		Hi,
		
		Emoke was right, these errors ('EntityManager must be access within a transaction') indeed were 
		caused by some previous, possibly swallowed exception. What happened was this:
		
		The business implementation was called by a dispatcher like so:
		
		         try {
		             List res = loadShippingPoints(orderby, asc, plantId);
		             return res;
		         }
		         catch (...) {
		           ... lots of exception handling here...
		         }
		         finally {
		             getDaoProvider().getDirectJpaDao().flush();
		             ThreadLocalUserInfo.setUserId(null);
		             OPLOG.logReturn(ex);
		         }
		
		... this is of course wrong because if there was an exception in the business code, the call 
		'getDaoProvider().getDirectJpaDao().flush()' fails as well and causes an exception, shadowing the 
		actual problem.
		
		I've changed the dispatchers in such a way that the flush() is only executed when the call to the 
		business method doesn't cause an exception.
		
		Valdas: for https://aww.adnovum.ch/ticketcenter/show_bug.cgi?id=ADN41194 there is now another error 
		that we (==me) must look into.
		
		Cheers,
		Alvi.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/etc/gdi/ejb3/templates/Dispatcher.java.vm

