Created On    : 08-May-2009 / alvi
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : PERSIST450: automatic project build of HOLCIM_LOGON failed (PMD checks)
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : 
		Date: Fri, 08 May 2009 07:38:51 +0200
		From: Christian Siffert <christian.siffert@adnovum.ch>
		User-Agent: Thunderbird 2.0.0.21 (X11/20090302)
		MIME-Version: 1.0
		To: =?ISO-8859-15?Q?G=E9rard_Roos?= <gerard.roos@adnovum.ch>, 
		 Alvaro Fussen <alvi@adnovum.hu>,
		 gabor.ginter@adnovum.ch
		Subject: Re: automatic project build of HOLCIM_LOGON failed
		[SNIP]
		
		Our guideline says (and here it is up-to-date , what a surprise ;-) ):
		======================================================================
		When should you use varargs? As a client, you should take advantage
		of them whenever the API offers them. Important uses in core
		APIs include reflection, message formatting, and the new printf
		facility.
		As an API designer, you should use them sparingly, only when the
		benefit is truly compelling, e.g. in tracing API's or for creating variable-
		formatted-messages for application specific exceptions.
		Do not overload a varargs method, or it will be difficult for programmers
		to figure out which overloading gets called.
		================================================================
		
		Hence I have a bug in adnant and I will throw out that pmd rule!
		Sorry, you will have to //NOPMD in the meanwhile, hope that works here. 
		
		-> it does
