Created On    : 08-May-2009 / zsolt
ADN Bugzilla  : ADN41188
ADN Change ID : SAPSERVICE111: make sapimport ready for bulk uploads (async/queuing)
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : I made the following changes:

		1) during processing an incoming SOAP-request for one of the SAP-webservices:
		   - information is stored in the staging area;
		   - the NEW_DATA_AVAILABLE_TS field of TLGNC_CRONSTATUS is set to the current 
		     time for the appropriate cron-job (cronstatus-entity).
		This way the information retrieved from the SOAP-request is stored in the staging 
		area and the proper cron-job is informed (triggered), that there is new data to 
		import from the staging area to logon-DB.

		2) a scheduled bean checks, if there is new data to import for the SAP-related cron-jobs. 
		In this very case the proper PL/SQL import-scripts are called one by one - in a predefined 
		sequence as there are dependencies between the imported entities.

		3) I had to put the checking of cronstatus-entities and the call for the PL/SQL 
		import-scripts into SEPARATE transactions. 
		Reason: 
			without making distributed transactions, we can not use 2 different datasources 
			in the same transaction (org.jboss.resource.connectionmanager.JBossLocalXAException).

Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

A logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/CronstatusServiceBean.java
