Created On    : 13-May-2009 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : PERSIST475: Fields to store contact person name and comment when signing order delivery via PDA
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : PDA allows to enter the "person" (text!) and also "comment",
		besides entering the signature (graphic). Where to store them in
		Logon DB?
Description   : In Workshop 13.5., the flow of data was clarified as follow:
		(for comment fields, additional text for delivery note, and contact person the same):
        1) User enters comment in the weborder -> not modifiable by others, kept
		2) Order managment reads them, and enters their own set of various
		   comments, and contact_person_txt. The values for these comments
		   get their initial values from the shipto & shipto-restriction.
		   (-> order & order_item)
		3) These comments land in the hands of the dispatcher. HIS comments
		   (CARRIER_DELIVERY_NOTE and CARRIER_TRUCK_DRIVER_NOTE) get the
		   initial value from the comments as left by the order manager
		   in step 2. He can modify if he wants, but he cannot modify the
		   comments in the fields as left by the order management in 2)
		4) The values of contact_person_txt and carrier_delivery_note
		   are the values which are sent to PDA, where they are shown
		   to the customer. He can accept or modify them (together with
		   signing. These values are stored in
		   - contact_person_signature_txt and
		   - CUST_DELIVERY_NOTE_COMMENT
		=> There is a FLOW represented by the set of various comments!
		=> Each step gets its initial values from the previous step,
		   and modifications only happen on the new fields (depending
		   on the status of the order as well).
		=> When an order goes back in the workflow, the comments fields
		   should be reset as well.
		PDF generation:
		- The origin of the fields 'contact person' / 'additional text for
		  delivery note' depends on the status of the order: If BEFORE
		  actually delivered (paper), take from 3), if AFTER the
		  delivery (PDA case), take from 4).
		  (Freedom of implementation: in the non-pda case, the values
		  from 3 can also copied into 4 directly - but check for sideeffects.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgnc_order.xml

