Created On    : 18-May-2009 / alvi
ADN Bugzilla  : https://aww.adnovum.ch/ticketcenter/show_bug.cgi?id=ADN41167
ADN Change ID : PERSIST483: GDI or some XML tool hates the string 'database' and cannot distinguish a tag from a value
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : we're much more stable now. unfortunately the really clean solution would require
		quite a lot of template-rewrites, but this solution is almost 100% robust and fool proof.
		solution:
		- from the xmlbean we get the table-xml-fragment
		- we path the control fields into that fragment
		- we path the '<xml-fragment>' tags to <table>
		- we check if there is any occurrence of 'xml-fragment' in the original xml
		  and trace and bail out. example:

     [java] 12:57:21,580 INFO  [     LogTool:27  ]
     [java] 12:57:21,582 INFO  [     LogTool:27  ] the file '/local/alvi/projects/logon/logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgnc_pool.xml'
     [java] 12:57:21,583 INFO  [     LogTool:27  ] contains the string 'xml-fragment'. please remove it as it is a reserved keyword.
     [java] 12:57:21,584 INFO  [     LogTool:27  ] (generating stopped)

		-> this is much more stable as there is probably no need for the xml to
		contain 'xml-fragment' ever. (whereas it is conceivable that the existing tags
		(e.g. table, database, etc) could be used out of context. This won't do any damage anymore)
		also: corrected a typo in logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgnc_pool_tx.xml
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgnc_pool_tx.xml
M logon-persistence/etc/gdi/mergexml/toolbox.xml
M logon-persistence/etc/gdi/mergexml/templates/merge_4all.xml.vm

