Description   : 1) Somehow JspC didn't like the common-web JAR on it's classpath. This
                JAR got on the classpath because of the new GDI tasks which require this
                JAR. <- update in GDI (GEN189).
                2) JspC complained about org.apache.commons.lang.StringUtils not being on
                the classpath because of (1), removed StringUtil references as they're not
                used in the JSPs.
                3) All JSPs got compiled in the same package, leading to duplicated
                classes, for example JsLibTile, now each project is compiled in a seperate
                package.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
