Created On    : 11-Jun-2009 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : 39784
ADN Change ID : PERSIST556: DB view for more flexible soldo-shipto search
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : Holcim wants to search for "Bieder 9000" and expects
        to find customer/shipto called '%Bieder%' in postal code 9000.
Description   : A prototype view has been described in the bug ticket,
        and basically approved by Christoph:
        - the order of the fields is NOT arbitrary (but people get
          used to it)
        - the search SHOULD be case insensitive, and use many wild-
          cards (beginning, end, all whitespace, all * explicitely
          addded by user)
Fix           : vlgns_soldship_flex_srch added. TODO: Marton, can
        you add this flexible search to the DISPOKARTE Search?
        Later, add in order search (but there are more cases), when
        we know about performance and issues. Maybe we need to
        add a materialized view fill fulltext search index on
        that composite_search_string.
        For the release 2009/2010 it shouldn't be an issue, as there
        are only ca 12000 shiptos. Oracle will do that in memory,
        and tests in SQL developer have shown very quick response
        times.
        (Additional fixes: synchronizing view mapping files with
        corrected DB.)
        MARTON: Sample queries are contained in custom_views.sql
        as well as in the ticket.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
