Created On    : 29-Jun-2009 / alvi
ADN Bugzilla  : https://aww.adnovum.ch/ticketcenter/show_bug.cgi?id=ADN42152
ADN Change ID : CFG121: Upgrade to jcan-log 1.4.0.0?
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : 
		"Should we upgrade to jcan-log 1.4.0.0? Advantages? Risks?"
		-> yes, we should. one of the major reason for me is that the latest version no longer loads
		the log4j-backend by way of calling Class.forName("...") in order to retrieve a log4j
		logger. This has caused lots of classloader related problems in other projects and it is 
		known that Class.forName() is broken in the JRE. (ClassLoader.loadClass() would be correct.)
		This alone is reason enough for the upgrade.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M config/build.properties

