Created On    : 24-Jul-2009 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : 44006
ADN Change ID : PERSIST651: Table tlgns_sap_netprice_order_item for 5th import interface
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : the 5th import interface sends data about the actual
		resulting net prices (net amount, rebate, tax, cash discount)
		for each order item that we sent to SAP earlier.
Description   : -
Fix           : Added table to store both original SAP values (as text,
		with leading zeros etc) and field for mapped value to tlgnc_order_item.
		Note, that the "header" data is stored redundant in each
		sap_netprice_order_item, on purpose.
		Alternative designs, and why rejected:
		- storing directly in additional fields tlgnc_order_item:
		  Bad, becuse import time of SAP gets lost on later modifications.
		  Also a mix between what belongs to Logon, and what to SAP domain.
		- storing sap_netprice_order + sap_netprice_order_item in 2 tables:
		  Most orders have exactly 1 item. for those, this table has no
		  use at all. There is always some undesired reduncancy, either
		  because of too many references or because the original sap header
		  fields are stored in each item (instead of just once).
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

A logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgns_sap_netprice_order_item.xml

