Created On    : 24-Jul-2009 / gerard
ADN Bugzilla  : 44026
ADN Change ID : CFG138, MOP228: PDA login not possible, fine-tuning initial config parameters
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : PDA login not possible
Description   : Non-unique RFID object label. Because of initial user load, pda
	user numbers are not only set but also swapped between existing users. The RFIDobject label
	job (RFIDServiceBean.syncRFIDLabels()) cannot handle such circular references, as for a
	temporary moment two identical labels must be possible.
Fix           :
	- Do not ensure rfid object label uniqueness during creation.
	unique constraint on rfidobjectlabel.object_label must be temporarily disabled on DB
	to fix such circular dependencies.

	- app.default.truck_route.TimeCorrectionFactor  = 1.2 (alt 1.5)
	- app.default.shipto.UnloadingTime_min = 30 (alt 20)
	- app.default.loadingpoint.LoadingTime_min = 15 (alt 18)
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/RFIDServiceBean.java
M logon-persistence/etc/csv/refdata/config.csv

