Created On    : 25-Aug-2009 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : TEST122, PERSIST692: Testdata for loadtest, enhanced data loader
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : Need 300 driver, assigned to a truck and a PDA device
Description   : -
Fix           : Description of the testdata:
		- Drivers have Name "AdN Person 001" - "AdN Person 300".
		- Their users have PDA user number "1000001" - "1000300".
		- Assigned to SAP Vendor 800040
		- Ext login "V800040-person001"-"V800040-person300"
		- Ext login password (non hashed...): "person001"-"person300"
		- Trucks: Number Plate "ADN 1000001" to "ADN 1000300", name "AdN Load 001"-"AdN Load 300"
		- Trucks also assigned to same vendor.
		- The Drivers are assigned to the truck with the same number:
		  "AdN Person 001" drives truck with plate "ADN 1000001"
		- PDA Devices: Are assigned to same vendor as well, and have
		  pda device numbers "ADN01000001" - "ADN01000300". (No
		  assignment done in "last_user_id".
		The data is generated exactly the same way as normal initialdata,
		and additional rows can easily added in Excel, with the autofill
		function (Excel enumerates mixed text/number fields correctly).
		Other changes:
		- tlgnu_user: pda logins moved from e.g. -110 to 100010
		  (negative numbers cause dups in rfid objects labels)
		- enhanced gdi templates to handle lookups for trailer/truck,
		  comments for differences in 1.0 and 1.1 DB model
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

A logon-persistence/etc/csv/loadtestdata/pda_device.csv
A logon-persistence/etc/csv/loadtestdata/truck.csv
