		Relevant for rail shippingpoints (wagons, maybe containers), but it could be
		used also for trucks: An entry defines how many loads (wagon, container,...)
		of a certain material are expected to be loaded per day at a shippingpoint.
		If no orders exist to be loaded, the system will consult this table and
		determine what pre-loading order could be created. If the number of loads
		loaded today (preloaded incl. used for customer orders) is reached, no
		pre-loading will happen anymore. The target_load_count can be exceeded but
		only by custom-orders, not with pre-loading orders.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

A logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgnc_shippingpoint_loadtarget.xml

