Created On    : 23-Oct-2009 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : 44699
ADN Change ID : PERSIST790: Introduced tlgnr_uom_bs.fuzzy_quantity_flag, needed when sending to parallel.
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : In the past, an amount which was 'vague' was sent to parallel
		with no net amount (meaning: fill with maximum). But if an explicit
		ton-value was known from ordered_uom_cd, that quantity was sent as
		an upper limit.
		With bug 44699 we added a 'convertible'(guessed) weight also to those
		vague UOM, and now they suddenly also have a weight.
		I don't know if send-to-parallel tries to convert all UOM in tons,
		or if it does a hardcoded check for "if UOM = 'to'", but in any
		case it is an information which should rather be added explicitely
		to the UOM.
Description   : -
Fix           : '15T','27T','36T','54T','LKW','BW','PAL','CON' are considered
		vague/fuzzy UOM, and their amount is not precise.
		The (old) 15T/27T/36T/54T are somewhoe in between, because they
		are a mix of type+UOM. But they are set as ctl_act_cd=0 anyway...
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgnr_uom_bs.xml
