Created On    : 18-Nov-2009 / matyas
ADN Bugzilla  : 45713
ADN Change ID : ADMIN629: executeUpdate functionality to handle expired session data 
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : OptimisticLockException
Description   : logon is not prepared for parallel entity modifications
Fix           : a javascript implementation is created for ExtJS calls to give the user the choice of updating the page or going back to the previous page in case an OptimisticLockException happens
				this change also contains some cleanup of useradmin javascripts
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : the solution made as generic as possible. For reuse you have to do the following:
				add executeUpdate.js to your page and initialize the executeUpdate object with its init method
				when you want to save the data, use the run method of executeUpdate like the following:
				executeUpdate.run(divId, saveUrl, saveParams, updateUrl, updateParams, exceptionRegexp, questionToAsk);
				where :
					divId : the divId which is loaded/updated after the request is processed
					saveUrl/Params : the normal action which needs to be executed
					updateUrl/Params : the action which updates the data of your page
					exceptionRegexp : the type of Exception which we try to handle
					questionToAsk : the question which will be shown to the user when the exception occurs. The user will have the option YES or NO, with YES the page will be updated, with NO the user ends up on the previous page with an Update button added to the div.
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-admin-web/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/admin/web/actions/useradmin/UserAdminAction.java
M logon-admin-web/src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/jsp/useradmin/SelfAdminDetail.jsp
