Created On    : 01-Feb-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 49850
ADN Change ID : PERSIST912, AUTH006: Generated authorizer adds prefix for normal entities
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : The problem was, that the generated authorizer simply added for example PlantBsEntity.ATTR_PLANT_CD
		to the query, which was resolved to PLANT_CD due to what an exception was thrown that
		PLANT_CD "column ambiguously defined". 
		With plant.plantCd reference the problem disappeared.
		From now instead PlantBsEntity.ATTR_PLANT_CD whateverEntity.ATTR_PLANT + "." + PlantBsEntity.ATTR_PLANT_CD
		is used.		
		On startup authorization itself is tested by calling dao.count(null). This run successfully before,
		and also after this change but since userId=1 was used for this test it did not really mean and does
		not mean too much. Run it with other user, who does have restrictions, but this also run successfully
		before and after the change too. In order to test this change if it really solves the problem
		we will need dao.cound(filter) instead of dao.count(null). In this case I suppose we will see that before
		the change if not null filter was given the test would fail, and hopefully after the fix
		nothing will fail. This needs some improvement in testing authorization.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/gdi/schema2ddlentities/templates/java/GeneratedAuthorizer.java.vm

