Created On    : 08-Feb-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 50497
ADN Change ID : PERSIST918: Wagon import now does attach created rfidobjects to the wagons fro which they are created for
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : This import should not be run on a db which already imported these wagons (not only because of breaking 
		unique constraint of object label, but also because of unique constraint of wagon no).
		To fix this problem on a db which already imported these wagons, but they are not attached to the wagon
		they were created for run the stored procedure update_cont_wagon_rfidobject (patch_1.2.0.4.sql contains it).
		That will try to fix this problem, and will succeed in case the wagon_no was not changed since the import).
		It will only update the reference only in case the rfidobject is type wagon, is not referenced at all, and the object 
		label is EXACTLY the same as the wagon_no of the wagon. As far wagon_no is not changeable in logon
		most likely the problem can be fixed easily.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/sql/initialdata/tlgnc_wagon_1.2.sql

