Created On    : 10-Feb-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 50772
ADN Change ID : ADMIN717: Table browser renders Boolean type fields with FlagTypeBean
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Distinction of flag dropdown based on Number(1,0) type proved to be wrong, since there are fields which are not
		flags, but have this type, such as for example NR_CHAMBERS of TLGNC_TRUCK or TLGNR_WAGON_TYPE_BS NR_CONTAINERS.
		From now Boolean type fields will use the new type renderer FlagTypeBean using FlagEditor.jsp, which will
		render the same input field with options (-),0,1 which was rendered until now for all fields
		having type Number(1,0).
		For the problematic field TLGNR_WAGON_TYPE_BS NR_CONTAINERS field correctly a Long java type field is 
		generated, so it is of course not a subject of FlagTypeBean, but of simple TypeBean, which renders
		a simple input field instead of a dropdown.
		The existing other typebeans are blob,date,readonly,timestamp,reference typebeans, none of them would interfere
		with this new typebean.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
