Created On    : 08-Mar-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 51255, 51774
ADN Change ID : ORDER984, BUSINESS1534, ORDERMGR040, COMMON303, TERMINAL016: Shipping terminal for bag changes
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : In case the load is related to bag order item, the input field netto is for the order items
		separately, even if they are merged into one load. They are going to be updated first, 
		and the endLoad will be called with the summed up quantity of the related items, just like for bulk.
		Endload is only changed for calls coming from source SYSTEM_TYPE_LOGON, because pda, and other sources
		do not pre-set the loaded quantities of the order items, but despite of this the current endLoad implementation
		may work for them if there is no shared load, since the loaded quantity will be equal to the load
		net quantity.
		For terminal a little more space given for UOM, since the translation may break the UI.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
