Created On    : 11-Mar-2010 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : 52004
ADN Change ID : PERSIST955: sapimport_log_cleanup: deleted in slices of 10000
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : After some huge SAP imports with tons of errors have occured
		(currently 9 Mio from Prod), the deletion of old tlgnc_log does
		no longer work because it results in a timeout.
		Even autonomous transactions did not work, because the deleted was
		supposed to run within 1 single transaction/commit. Besides of the
		timeout issues, there was also not enough TEMP tablespace on a
		typical DB instance.
		More analysis and examples from Holcim Test env: see ticket 52004
Fix           : Introduce delete in slices.
		Also, recommended to reduce the max lifetime of errors. 28 days
		is too long for errors which keep repeating...
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/sql/logon_log_pkg.sql

