Created On    : 25-Mar-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 48701
ADN Change ID : TERMINAL027, PKG103, SETUP113, CFG191, BUSINESS1554: Login module using pda user no as user name and passcode as password
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : The terminal login module is placed in the DMZ login module, there was no need to copy the whole, as not much would be different
		there. The access is denied in case someone wants to switch to order or admin, because the authorizedUserDenominator is defined as TerminalUsers and 
		not Users what the normal login module sets for the logged in user. Therefore it is not possible to switch between terminal 
		and other parts of the application.
		The login-config of the terminal has one special option terminal-mode, which is true in this case. Depending on this, the username
		and the password will be checked against the users pda_user_no and pickup_barcode_passcode combination, and not ext login and password.
		The login module though cannot preserve the loadingpoint request parameter of the request url, thus we needed to store it in a cookie
		which is then read in case the login fails. Using this cookie the failed login can also go back to the first login screen.
		The cause why it was needed is that we did not wanted to change the login module or anything serious just for storing this pre-setting
		of the url.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M config/build.properties
M etc/login-config.xml
M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/DmzServiceBean.java
