Created On    : 12-Apr-2010 / cosmin
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : PERSIST983: Throw Exception on null Expression in FilterImpl.add()
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Passing null as any parameter in a factory method of the class Restrictions
				causes the method to return null. FilterImpl.add() ignores calls having null
				as a parameter, thus ignoring the Restriction intended by the client code.
				This can cause the generated query to be less restrictive than intended by 
				the caller, ingnoring something that is most likely a bug.
				If the behaviour of ignoring Restrictions havin null as a parameter is intended
				(e.g. if a search parameter is not provided by the user), please implement this 
				explicitely in the caller code.
				IMPORTANT: As we don't know how many places in the code will be affected by this 
				new exception (be it because of a bug or as an intended effect), this change 
				might be removed from the next release, if it has a too big impact.
Fix           : FilterImpl.add() has been modified to throw a NullPinterException if the input
				parameter is null.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/src/main/java/ch/nevis/gdi/jpa/filter/FilterImpl.java

