Created On    : 13-Apr-2010 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : 52706
ADN Change ID : PERSIST989: Add is_repair_flag to tlgnr_maint_type_bs
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : No distinction Rep/Main possible in the critical area
		of sending to SAP->SBB (SBB needs this. Probably refuses to
		transport broken wagons, unless marked clearly as "repair"
		transportation order.)
Description   : -
Fix           : Necessary to distinguish Material/NHM Code when sending
		to SAP (->SBB):
		TLGNR_WAGON_TYPE_BS.REPAIR_SAP_MATERIAL_NO
		TLGNR_WAGON_TYPE_BS.MAINTENANCE_SAP_MATERIAL_NO
		Rule, see DB comment of new field:
		
		Repair-Type Flag. In many places of the application it does not
		matter if a maintenance is a true (planned) maintenance, or actually
		an (unplanned) repair, but in some cases (transportation by the rail
		company) it does. Evaluation logic in tlgnc_order_rep_maint_type:
		If at least ONE type has IS_REPAIR_FLAG set, the whole order counts
		as repair.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgnr_maint_type_bs.xml
