Created On    : 26-May-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 54182, 54328, 54200
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS1642, ORDER1122: Change of sequence in sending to sap, changes because of truck container terminal case, changes in delivered fields for bag
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Changes in sending to SAP: Sending to SAP happened before freezing the order, which had a higher risk to fail for some reason, but the message has already been sent to 
		SAP. As a result sending to SAP happaned more times, since the changes did not take place in Logon due to the rollback at the end.
		As far sending the message throws exception if the send fails, that will undo the changes in the service anyway, therefore theoretically it is
		secured that if the sending fails, changes do not take place in logon either. Therefore changing the sequence in credit note sending phase2 (until now:
		send then freeze and save credit note, from now: freeze, set timestamp, save credit note and then send). Same applies for normal sending to SAP.
		Changes due to truck container terminal:
		Truck container terminal case: closeAfterload was designed to set the order to delivered in case the truck does not have a pda and has no chance to 
		send the unloading time and such after loading. Until now it set the unloading_ts right at loading when it was closed right at loading.
		As far the truck container terminal lists the containers according to the rules: the load is loaded, but not
		yet unloaded (! unloading_ts must be null), has a container, does not have truck/trailer and the container's last known shippingpoint is the same shippingpoint from where
		the truck has to fetch the container, and material matches - if the closeafterload sets the unloading_ts, it is not possible to fetch
		the container at the container terminal, although it is delivered and left there. Therefore from now closeafterload will NOT set the unloading_ts for the 
		load if the shipto is a container terminal, it will just do everything except this.
		As agreed if the container is left at the container terminal, its truck and trailer_id must be cleared together with the container's composition, therefore
		this will also happen in closeafterload in case the shipto is a container terminal.
		Changes in delivered fields of bag items: from now the delivered uom and quantity is calculated to the base uom of the material, and that is going to be set
		into the order item.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/CreditNoteServiceBean.java
M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/OrderServiceBean.java
