Created On    : 14-Jun-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 54954
ADN Change ID : ORDER1142, BUSINESS1667: Order detail cost calculation change costs are updated when recalculate is pressed
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Until now order detail did NOT save the changes to the costs, either if there was an error, or costs could
		be determined successfully the costs were not changed in the db. It was told to be only a tool to check if 
		calculation would succeed.
		The ticket itself was only about pickup, but in the meantime it turned out that the recalculation of costs
		does have to save the new costs, and even make sure that if the calculation is UNsuccessful then the frozen 
		tables REPORT_FINISHED_COMM_FLAG must be set to false in case the calculation became unsuccessful after a
		certain change, and cost recalculation.
		How order detail has to work after the change:
		Case 1: When clicking recalculate costs: if cost calculation fails there must be an error message signaling the failure
		with the exact problem - just as until now - but not as before, the costs which are missing have to show Error
		on the commercial tab, signing that the cost could not be determined. In any case the frozen tables must be updated
		if the calculation was successful then  REPORT_FINISHED_COMM_FLAG must be true, otherwise false, and the costs 
		have to be saved to the frozen tables as well. Summarized: click on recalculate: recalculate costs, set the invalid ones
		to zero, and the freeze the order. As a result if costs are valid  REPORT_FINISHED_COMM_FLAG will be true, otherwise false.
		The null cost values will show which are the problematic ones, and the error message will give a hint what was missing
		in order to have a successful calculation.
		Case 2: When bp is modified (there is a button Override BP which will update certain, and crucial fields of the order and 
		also the frozen table), the costs have to be recalculated, and the costs have to be refreshed in the db just as if 
		one would click recalculate costs right after modifying the BP. 
		Step by step: click Override BP, change another business partner, click hinzufugen, and then one saves the order, the
		following things will happen: try to update the costs, null the erroneous ones, freeze the order and then save the order.
		If cost calculation failed, the same happens as if recalculate would happen: invalid costs will be nulled, and 
		frozen tables  REPORT_FINISHED_COMM_FLAG will be set accordingly.
		Regarding transactions: if cost calculation fails there must be an error message, but the update of the order have to happen
		and the frozen table must be updated as well ( REPORT_FINISHED_COMM_FLAG will be set to false).
		If the update of order fails costs and frozen tables must remain as they were though.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/ContributionCalcServiceBean.java
