Created On    : 06-Jul-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 56212
ADN Change ID : SAPSERVICE148, PERSIST1026: Change of SAP import to set valid_from_dat and valid_to_dat correctly, added update sql script
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Until now the hour:minute:second part of the valid_to_dat field of both condition tables (tlgns_sap_mat_cond,
		tlgns_sap_transport_cond) was not set, therefore it was saved as 00:00:00, and as sap sent the valid from date
		of the next period as the next day, the valid_to_dat was a day when no valid order condition was available,
		therefore not possible to create order on that day.
		Changed SAP import to save the valid_to_dat as the last second of the day: 23:59:59 and save the valid_from_dat
		as the first minute 00:00:00 of the day SAP sent.
		Added sql script, which updates the valid_to_dat to 23:59:59 if it was 00:00:00 (same day as before). The update
		script is supposed to update the ctl_mod_ts to the date of running the script, and update the ctl_tcn (increment by 1)
		and set the ctl_mod_uid to the system user (1).
		Tested SAP import, valid_to_dat was 23:59:59 as it was intended.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/sql/sapimport_cond_pkg.sql
A logon-persistence/etc/sql/patch/1.4.0/ADN56212_update_condition_table_valid_to_dates.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/patch/1.4.0/patch_1.4.0.sql

