Created On    : 15-Jul-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 55882
ADN Change ID : PERSIST1037, COMMON367, BUSINESS1684, ADMIN767: Renaming of field parallel_ls_id of tlgnc_loadingpoint to weigh_system_loadingpoint_no, handlers changed accordingly
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : From now LogonEventRequestHandlers using loadingpointno will use the type cd as filter parameter in order to load the loadingpoint for a certain request. 
		Parallel_rail uses parallel_rail type, logon_services uses wewas, parallel_truck uses parallel).
		This is all fine until this rule still holds, that there is no request which can arrive from any of these sources, but from a loadingpoint, which is not with type written above. 
		(It could happen for pda request handler - loadingpoints taking part in pda requests can also be parallel and other types -, but that uses the rfid object 
		label in order to load the loadingpoint instead of getting it for plantcd + loadingpointNo).
		Shippingpoint master data screen still guarantees that for a parallel server there is only one loadingpoint with weighSystemLoadingpointNo. For loadingpoint types, which do not use
		praallel system (have no parallel spid) it is only guaranteed that only one active loadingpoint with weighSystemLoadingpointNo and type can exists PER SHIPPINGPOINT. That also 
		means it is NOT guaranteed that per plant there is only one such loadingpoint.	
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
