Created On    : 28-Jul-2010 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 57312
ADN Change ID : PERSIST1059, SAPSERVICE154: Transport condition import changes related to MVGR2 field
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Transport condition import sets marked_for_deletion field to 1 (overwriting the value received from
		SAP in field LOEVM_KO) in case the additional field MVGR2 contains something else than GRA, and besides
		updates the pricingconditionsreqdt table's field of the request to 4 (imported, but set to deleted/ignored).
		The logic is: if there is a field MVGR2 for a transport condition it cannot be anything else than GRA. The additional field
		is only supposed to come for transport condition ZTF099, but if SAP sends it for other condition type
		it will also set the marked_for_deletion flag, and on the other hand if ZTF099 does NOT contain the field, 
		the import might be successful, although it did not contain the field MVGR2 though it was supposed to
		contain it. Assumption is that SAP will stick to the rules they defined, MVGR2 will be always sent for
		ZTF099 and only that, and will NOT be sent for other transport conditions.
		Note that the rule is only for TRANSPORT conditions, and is NOT added for material conditions, as far there
		none of the conditions is supposed to contain the field MVGR2, therefore no need to add this ignore logic there.
		Updated tlgns_sap_transport_cond marked_for_deletion comment to be visible that it might mean that it is set to
		deleted because of this ignore logic, and not because SAP deleted it.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgns_sap_transport_cond.xml
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/sapimport_cond_pkg.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/patch/1.4.0/patch_1.4.0_sap.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/refdata/tlgnr_sapimpstatus.sql

