Created On    : 31-Jul-2010 / gergely
ADN Bugzilla  : 56597, 56613
ADN Change ID : ORDER1158, BUSINESS1701: Refactoring for the Sap Material Condition handling
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : I. Refactoring for the displaying of the price in Order Taking:     

		The old conditionsMap JS map on the client side is eliminated, the price 
		label (rate + currency) is now sent by the server in the OrderTakingEditorDto 
		(result of the OrderAjaxService.getCollectedEditorData() call) from the server 
		to the browser, when the user modifies the product, delivery type, or supply 
		plant, since these might affect the displayed price. 
		
		
		II. Refactoring of the SAP Material Price condition evaluation for:
		- Order taking
		- Web-order taking
		- Pickup
		- CreateOrderRequestHandler
		The code is more reasable now, and the supply plant and distribution channel
		are taken into account.
		
		The main steps of the evaluation are the following now:
		
		1. List<SapMatCondEntity> condList = DispokarteService.fetchSapMatCond(SareaBsEntity sarea, SapBpEntity soldtoSapBp, SapBpEntity shiptoSapBp). 
		This is called only once, when a given page is loaded, and contains all 
		conditions which might be valid for a certain combination of product/delivery 
		type/supply plant/zone during the order creation. The list is stored on the 
		Struts form tipically.
		
		2. SapMaterialConditionsUtil.selectPriceCondition(List<SapMatCondEntity> condList, Long sapMatId, String trspModeCd, String plantCd, String trspZoneCd)
		This method selects the "best" condition (based on the parameters and priority) 
		from the previously created list. In order taking, the method is 
		called every time when the user changes either the material, delivery type, 
		supply plant, or the zone. In the webservice, it is called only once.
		
		For the transport conditions, the changes were minor: only a filter for the distribution channel 
		has been added to the methods in DispokarteService.

		TODO 1: The new price handling is not done yet in dispokarte (and the existing code there is possibly displaying incorrect prices since a long time, but not sure)
		TODO 2: Just saw recently that the order cloning became broken because of the changes. Needs to be analyzed how much code should be changed there to fix it.

Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
