---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Created On    : 17-Sep-2010 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : 59613
ADN Change ID : PERSIST1104: Changing seq for NGE, treat pool as initial (not refdata)
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : the external order number is used also in CHE, not just NGE.
		Same as for all other sequences.
		Sequences which were ONLY in custom_sequences would not be executed
		=> need to be in patch for CHE!
Description   : -
Fix           : Tried to make all sequences consisten, according to this description in clean_DB_for_NGE.
    - CHE: All technical sequences are         1'000 - ...
    - NGE: All technical sequences are 1'000'000'000 - ...
    - CHE: Normal orders are in a special range given from SAP:    10'000'000 - 19'999'999.
    - NGE: Normal orders simply start in the middle of that range: 15'000'000 - 19'999'999.
      (Think about collisions/out of numbers later...)
    - CHE: External order numbers should start outside, to avoid confusions. Set to 1'000'000.
      Note that these are independent of SAP.
	- NGE: Similar to normal orders: start at 1'500'000
      -> 0.5 Mio orders until collision with NGE should be enough.
         On top, if this happens, that would give us experience on what to do
         if the SAP range is getting too small. Which will be much more critical...
    Then, treated pool as real initialdata (not refdata), more consistent.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/database/tables/tlgnc_ext_order.xml
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/custom_sequences.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/nge_initialdata/tlgnc_pool.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/patch/1.4.0/clean_DB_for_NGE.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/patch/1.4.0/external_orders.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/patch/1.4.0/initialdata_load_NGE_1.4.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/patch/1.4.0/patch_1.4.0.sql

