Created On    : 30-Sep-2010 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : PERSIST1121: utility for missing mat_plant entries should respect only PROD plants
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : mat_plant is only wanted for PROD plants. It is not a problem
		if entries are entered also for SUPPLY plants, but they are never
		used by LOGON, and it would just lead to additional maintenance
		efforts (for no benefit): On delivery notes + prod cost calculations
		etc it's always the production plant which influences the selection.
Description   : -
Fix           : The previous version of VLGNS_UTIL_MATPLANT_MISSING would
		lead to many bogus errors (for all SUPPLY plants as well, because
		SAP does not distinguish this in tlgns_sap_material_plant.
		Worse: The script in sapimportmat.add_dummy_mat_plants would create
		too many entries.
		Therefore, added a filter "and production_plant = 1" to the view,
		which will also influence the add_dummy_mat_plants.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/sql/custom_views.sql

