Created On    : 28-May-2011 / nemes
ADN Bugzilla  : ADN70757
ADN Change ID : SAPSERVICE197: Holcim Logon/Ifc: SAP: Re-evaluate/Adapt current IN coming SAP Interface for new XSD files
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : added functionality to cutomize hyperjaxb's built in naming scheme
			1) separate src/class dir for the customization 
				(logon-webservices/src/ext/java, 
				 logon-webservices/build/classes/ext/classes)
			2) shortcut for xjc classpath in build.xml (xjc.classpath)
			3) the generate-entities target now has a builtin javac
				to compile our cutomization classes
			4) added the new classes and config to the xjc taskdef
			5) proveded new configuration file, to override the original
				hyperjaxb3 bean config file, and inject our naming
				implementation (logon-webservices/etc/cfg/hyperjaxb3.config.xml)
			6) our new config file is applied on top of the original, which is in the jar
				${HYPERJAXB3_HOME}dist-src/lib/hyperjaxb3-ejb-plugin-0.3.jar
					at
				org/jvnet/hyperjaxb3/ejb/plugin/applicationContext.xml
					(uses sring to autowire the bean difinitions)
			7) the new naming class is called: 
				com.holcim.logon.xjc.hyperjaxb3.NamingExt
					and it does some logging, using jcan-log
					(which is also added to the xjc.classpath)
			8) updatedotclasspath is augmented, so eclipse will have no problems
				providing java editor to our new class

Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-webservices/build.xml
M logon-webservices/properties.xml
A logon-webservices/etc/cfg/hyperjaxb3.config.xml
A logon-webservices/src/ext/java/com/holcim/logon/xjc/hyperjaxb3/NamingExt.java

