Created On    : 29-Jul-2011 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 72757, 72505
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS1966, COMMON453, ORDER1347, TERMINAL054: Switching from condition based to contract based delivery possibilities
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Delivery settings are from now loaded at a centrac place in ShiptoSalesAreaUtil and using that
		maps to resolve the valid delivery possibilities are loaded. Dispokarte uses these loaded lists, and
		also call center uses them.
		In case problematic the restrictions created sooner can be loaded, and order creation should be possible
		still with those settings. If you do not uncomment that, only those materials will be available in call center
		which have contract reference.
		  ShiptoSalesAreaUtil row 347
			/**
			 * HERE ACTIVATE THE USAGE OF EXISTING CH RESTRICTIONS, WHICH WERE BASED ON MATERIAL CONDITIONS
			 * FOR TESTING PURPOSES IT CAN BE USEFUL!
			 * For now DO not load restrictions not based on contracts!
			 */
		Weborder and pickup terminal does not know anything about contracts it still requires restrictions to exist.
		Known issues: Orders with multiple bag products cannot be saved.
		Basic ideas: Delivery settings can  be based on contracts and also on restrictions, but they still need to be
		valid against the core logon and sap data, and that is made sure by using a common place.
Fix           : -
