---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Created On    : 13-Sep-2011 / romek
ADN Bugzilla  : ADN75319
ADN Change ID : ORDER1387: Creating a customer user with sarea restr. but no company code restr causes exception
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : -
Fix           : The original implementation made all Sales Areas assignable
				when there were no assigned Company Codes. However,
				the specification requires that the user account cannot be
				assigned to any Sales Areas when no Company Code is
				assigned. Therefore, I fixed this. Additionally,
				originally method fetchSareasForCompCodeList in
				UserAdminServiceBean fetched every Sales Areas when
				the passed Company Code list was empty. This supported
				the behaviour written above, however, it also introduced
				an additional bug: because the method is also called after
				the removal of a company code, if you removed a Company
				Code when it was the only one selected, you passed an empty
				list again, resulting in that the Sales Area belonging to
				that Company Code was not removed either. I fixed that too.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-admin-web/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/admin/web/actions/useradmin/UserAdminAction.java
M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/UserAdminServiceBean.java

