Created On    : 08-Nov-2011 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 77128
ADN Change ID : ADMIN903, BUSINESS2098: Transfer delivery document sending - two documents (inbound + outbound) are going to be sent
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : tlgnr_sap_contract_type_bs.contract_is_stpo_flag: 'Based on this information, it is decided if a delivery document (SalesDoc)
		in the case of a Contract or a Transfer delivery document is sent to SAP'. 
		This flag is on, and only for these ON for stock transfer purchase order (STPO) and scheduling agreement (SA) contract types.

		From now on it implicitely means if this flag is on, that two transfer delivery documents have to be sent for the contract type:
		an inbound and an outbound, and there is only a few fields which differ for the two cases (See ticket 77128 in what they differ exactly,
		and also SAP interface specification of LRQ082).

		When sending SAP outbound transfer delivery document (see LRQ 041 Determinig when 
		transaction is sent to SAP chapter of O2C spec) actually two requests will be sent out to SAP an inbound and an outbound request. 
		The timestamp of sending is intended to be set in case both are sent successfully.

		There is no validation regarding field /transfer_delivery_creation/item_general_data/WERKS in case it is left empty,
		error will be logged: 'No plant_cd is specified for the shipto. /transfer_delivery_creation/item_general_data/WERKS field 
		is going to be left empty in the inbound transfer delivery document. [ShiptoId=...]' shipto sap id, etc.

		Test tab had been adapted to the double message, from now there are two options: inbound and outbound options
		retrieved for the same order.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
