Created On    : 14-Nov-2011 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : 72772
ADN Change ID : TEST392, ADMIN906, PERSIST1477, SIMUL058: Reorganization of tests attempt to make common code parts available for workflow tests
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Test util: created LogonExtSelenium, which can be used for common ext usage in Logon. Replaced selenium references to this
		subclass, from now on all tests can reach these ext functions like typing in an ext combobox selecting nth row, etc.
		Introduced new testcase type which is to be extended CallCenterTestCase, this file should be extended in case a test case
		needs to use the call center screen.

		Introduced new testcase pattern PropertyTransferTest. For this kind of tests there is an input file from where the properties
		are read and there is an export file to where all the properties read when starting the test case, and all which had been added
		while running the test are added. Workflow tests are using this pattern, have a constant input property file which contains
		the ids on what the test case can be based, and add further properties to the output file.
		It is not yet sure that this pattern is good, it was introduced because of soapui, but soapui tests should rather receive ids,
		from Logon requests rather than using a property file. For the moment it is the first step trying to get out of the property
		chaos which was present in all these tests.

		Master data test had been separated to different test classes: shippingpoint, truck + trailer. Most of them were uncommented,
		now reactivated. Shippingpoint testcase had been extended to create a shippingpoint, with sap number SEL1, this shippingpoint is
		supposed to be deleted at the end of the test in order that the test is repeatable in each nightly build.

		TruckTrailerTest had rfid admin functions, which was not working at all, for the moment removed the rfid part, those
		can be readded later.

		User admin selenium test: still not fixed, probably should rather be removed, as most likely it is doing the same as 
		user authorization test. That test is activated, but it is shorter than it was sooner, probably parts were removed sooner for some reason.
		The user admin tests could be extended more.

		Removed Workflow09Test because it was very old, and was not running since a long time, and most likely was doing either 2009 
		workflow, which is most likely Ch parallel single road order test.

		In PERSIST added test data in negative range for external materials and external sites for adza testdata. They are used in the external workflow.
  
		In minimal setup changed rfidobjects for the test trucks Truck 1 (C1) etc. as those were not in sync with the rfidobject label 
		generation rules.

		In workflow tests the input parameters are no longer based on order search as it makes the test unpredictable. In the meantime did not
		remove that functionality, probably we can use it to look for test data, and or release an order search test, or something.

		In integration soapui tests disabled test steps in external workflow test startLoadMop and endLoadMop because they were run after
		the successful external order test, and they left in fact the order in an inconsistent state leaving the assignment's status code
		as 'loading'.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
