		FIXME: Update patch and Dbs (preschedulers should get both roles: pool manager and scheduler to make sure that they can use prescheduling functionality)

		Business (affects order, and admin as well): 

		1. Order detail commercial and executing carrier dropdowns
		    Order detail service now only retrieves commercial for commercial and executing for executing carriers
		    TODO test: if the carrier stored on the order is invalid, it should still be shown!

		2. Removing parameter isPrescheduler
		   With removin prescheduler role also removed sending this boolean value in order service functions -> affects admin, order, cust as well

		3. Prevention to set invalid commercial and/or executing carriers on order
		   Added new exception type to be thrown in case of an invalid update of carrier attribute of the order. Results in Fenics 10701 error.
		
		Order services (Fenics):
		1. Truck specified does not belong to the executing carrier specified on order
		    code: 10701
		    message: Truck assignment not possible (Scheduled and actual truck belong to different carriers, order = xy)
		
		2. added exception: the order belongs to a tour assignment
		    code: 10701
		    message: Truck assignment not possible (Unsupported state: the order is scheduled to be part of a truck tour.Assignment id=xy)
  
		3. real truck does not belong to an executing carrier:
		    code: 10701
		    message: Truck assignment not possible (The carrier specified as executing carrier is not an executing carrier. Order id=xy; order number=xy)

		TODO test: transaction boundaries if messages sent to Fenics are in sync with the order in Logon in these cases + describe how it leaves the order.

		Scheduling action:
		1. Executing carrier should show all available executing carriers, and authorization should not apply there.

		Scheduling js:
		1. Java script fix
		   Truck scheduling screen ext js bug due to usage of nobr tag. Only showed up in IE8. According to Roland it was working in IE9, and for sure
		   working in Firefox. In the meantime in IE8 it completely blocked usage if at least one truck was present on the screen, which belonged to
		   a carrier, who required prescheduling.
		   Also present in 2.0.0.6. reference.

		2. Changes due to removal of prescheduler role
		  2a. Drag and drop rules: depending on the commercial/executing carrier setting of the order/assignment.
		  2b. Release functionality: depending on having only scheduler or also pool role.
