Created On    : 30-Jan-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-4554
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2145: When to send cancel to Fenics policy change
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Sending cancel to Fenics weighing system policy has been changed according to the following rules below:

		1. Deleting order: 

		1.a. if order has assignment (deallocate and delete only that order from the assignment if exists)
		  send a cancel: yes (anyway (even if there is or there is no plan in the background)
		  keep planning data: yes (the order might be deleted by the customer, or anyone else, but not the holcim planner)

		1.b. order does not have an assignment
		  send a cancel: yes (anyway even if there is or there is no plan in the background)
		  keep planning data: yes (the order might be deleted by the customer, or anyone else, but not the holcim planner)

		2. Deallocate whole assignment
		  send cancel: only if the order is not dispatched, and there is no planning data (NOTE: here I did not know what statuses should also not
		  send cancel like loading? arrived at loadingpoint? etc. in 2.0.0.6 there was no limitation regarding it, and the only thing that I
		  am aware of is that in status dispatched it should NOT send cancel for sure so for now exclude only dispatched statuse from sending cancel).
		  keep planing data: yes (always)
		
		3. set order pool on scheduling screen (implicit rejectbypool)
		  send a cancel: only if there was a plan in the background
		  keep planning data: NO, never (as was until now, the holcim planner does this, and he expects the planning data to be deleted!)

		4. reject by pool
		  send a cancel: only if there was a plan in the background
		  keep planning data: NO, never (as was until now, the holcim planner does this, and he expects the planning data to be deleted!)

		5. reallocate (on scheduling screen move in status transmitted to truck, or trigger selectOrderLoading from Fenics):
		  send cancel: never 
		  send order notification with the new truck: 
			 yes, if triggered from scheduling screen
			 no, if triggered from Fenics (the weighing system is the initiator)

		For CHE these rules also hold, and they will be OK, as in the swiss system there is no planning at all.
		
		Added additional check when setting executing carrier: if the commercial carrier is not specified it should not be possible
		to set the executing carrier!
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
