Created On    : 26-Mar-2012 / nemes
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-4688
ADN Change ID : WSCLIENT130, BUSINESS2194: LOGON-CHE-P: CPU S027 100% - possibly caused by network errors -> leaking?
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : serviceStub._getServiceClient().cleanupTransport() wsa not called,
		this way webservices without a response (sap) could have issues
		with the way how axis2 uses HttpClient (MultiThreadedConnectionManager
		used with new HttpClient instance for every request).
		When the connection was not estabilished on a low-level (http) axis2
		returned without releasing the resources (java/op system socket).
Fix           : called cleanup transport, also added some code to be able to reuse HttpClient
		with a newer axis2 version (it does not work well in 1.6.0)
		Refactored several classes to be a bit more distinct from each other
		(separate logic), and to favor immutability wherever possible.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

