Created On    : 29-Mar-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-4596
ADN Change ID : PERSIST1623, ORDER1539, BUSINESS2198, COMMON563: Order log related changes
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : **************** Removing generation of audit events ****************************

		Order auditing was until now generated. Generation of this code will be removed, as it was not
		clear enough and auditing is rather going to the direction which rather needs not generatable
		code, and it would be an overhead to maintain code generation.

		Until 2.0.0.8 auditing was only saving values if they changed. Due to the required order log display
		requirements it was necessary to store a state of a field even if it has not changed, there is two possible
		use cases for that, please see documented in the specification linked in the ticket.


		********************************  Deallocation bizevent storing changes ************************************************

		In 2.0.0.8 it resulted in a deallocate event for the assignment -> the deallocate appeared for all the orders belonging currently for the assignment
		which is not really correct, but probably acceptable.

		From now on a deallocate will result in a bizevent per order -> correct because if the assignment is still active the event will only appear for
		the specific order, and not all orders which are still with the assignment.

		To keep the current logic if the assignment is completely inactivated (all orders removed) Logon will store a last deallocate event only belonging
		to the assignment (reason: cannot be sure if this event was on purpose, and was used somewhere).

		Thusly Logon will anyway have a bizevent per order to link an assignment with an order, and can consider all events of the assignment before
		the deallocation transitively belonging to the order -> additional bizevents loaded for the linked assignment(s).


		************************************************ Using deallocation bizevent on the order log ************************************************
		
		In 2.0.0.8 order log bizevents were loaded as followings: all bizevents 
		      belonging to the order itself (ignoring also assignment attribute)
		      belonging ONLY to the ACTIVE assignment (order_id null)

		From now on first query:
		      belonging to the order itself (ignoring also assignment attribute)
		      belonging ONLY to the ACTIVE assignment (order_id null)

		If within these bizevents deallocate event is to be found then construct or filter for that: all events for ONLY that assignment before the 
		deallocation and run second query.

		Second query: 
		      belonging to the order itself (ignoring also assignment attribute)
		      belonging ONLY to the ACTIVE assignment (order_id null)
		      belonging ONLY to the assignment before deallocation from that assignment


		************************************************ Bizevent creation changes ************************************************

		New bizevent type: commercial carrier refuse (127)
		Using until now existing but not used bizevents: transmitted to commercial carrier (104), transmitted to commercial carrier ack (105)
		
		Changed actions related to:
		1. set pool
		  from now creates one set pool event (enhancement 1)
		  note: left transmit to pool as-is: stores set pool event
		2. transmit to commercial carrier: 
		  until now: stored set commercial carrier event (120)
		  from now: stores transmit to commercial carrier (104)
		3. commercial carrier rejects
		  until now: bizevent type set commercial carrier (120)
		  from now: bizevent type commercial carrier refuse (127)
		4. set commercial carrier
		  until now: no event stored
		  from now on: store bizevent type set commercial carrier (120)
		5. deallocate: please see section 'Deallocation bizevent storing changes'

		Others please find in the documentation attached to the ticket.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
