Created On    : 31-May-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-4898
ADN Change ID : ORDER1604: Selected order item's editability should not affect other items editability
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : WAS: When the material tab was rendered, editability rules were determined by the selected order item, and if for the
		      selected order item it was determined that a certain field is editable it was applied for the corresponding field of 
		      the other items.

		      Example: ordered quantity of the selected item (1) is editable according to the rules -> enable all other item's (2,3) ordered quantity
			       ordered quantity of the selected item (2) is not editable according to the rules -> disable all other item's ordered quantity (1,3)
		      
		      This was not really noticable until now (?), as most of the items are handled mostly together regarding weighing. According to the LRQ 017.1 Advaced Services
		      services are distinguished, and their editability for sure should not apply on other items of the order, even though their rules currently are
		      quite similar to the editability rules of other order items.

		IS: Technically: when evaluating jsp, apply the selected order item's rules only for the row corresponding with the selected item number. For others by default
			 disable the fields when rendering, but make the parameters reachable for the javascript run when clicking on the material radio button
			 to set the row's fields properly, but only when the radio button is selected.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-order-web/src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/jsp/auftrag/orderdetail/MaterialTab.jsp
