Created On    : 01-Jun-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-4581
ADN Change ID : ORDER1607: For services also use the two flags to determine if basic editability of loaded fields are enabled
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Editability of loaded quantity and UOM depends on two fundamental things not depending on bag/bulk:

		  1. tare weights are not null stored on the load (tareNetWeightsAreNotNullFlag)
		  2. load is in 1-1 relationship with the order item (if not, then the shared  load should not be possible to be changed, 
			only the loaded, and therefore the delivered fields of the order item. (orderItemAndLoadRel11Flag)

		In the case of services these requirements will be set as following:

		tareNetWeightsAreNotNullFlag: As there is no load to check for tare weight being set, consider all statuses above and including loaded as a possible 
		    candidate. The specification required also that deleted order can also be changed, therefore it applies also for deleted.
		orderItemAndLoadRel11Flag: as there is no load, consider it always false -> will behave as shared load items, loaded quantity editable

		Change for new items (currently only services, later on might be other types as well?):
		If the order item is not persisted, and it does not have an id yet, ordered quantity must be possible to be able to specify -> if the itembean 
		contains a new not persisted item, always allow editing of the ordered fields.

		Bugfixes: 
		1. javascript error when changing loaded quantity for a fresh created service item, cause: it has no id. For new items the id of the
		   orderitembean (not the entity) will be set to a unique value to guarantee as less change as possible, and in the meantime be able to use. 
		   (Leftover from the ticet)
		2. Save failure if empty ordered quantity is given. Now save is prevented with a warning message.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

