Created On    : 23-Jul-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-4752
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2317, PERSIST1797, TEST441: Landfill PDA, and assignment part data storing changes
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Creation of assignment parts changes for landfill as follows:
		  1. loading part will NOT get the reference to the shippingpoint, but to the ship-to, 
		      as that is the point where the assignment part's event will happen

		  2. drive-to part will not get the reference to the ship-to, but it will get
		      the FK reference to the shippingpoint as that is the place where th
		      assignment part's event will happen
  
		  3. unloading part will not get the reference to the ship-to, but will fet FK reference
		      to the shippingpoint as that is the place where the assignment part's event willhappen

		  4. no return assignment part will be created as the unloading happens at the plant (shippingpoint)

		  5. finished assignment part's planned start is calculated as: unloading's planned start + unload
		      duration (not as for the normal orders where it is: returning part's planned start + transport
		      duration)

		Explanation: With switching the foreign key references made it sure that the to outgoing request handler is sending
		the relevant point id, and point coordinate as follows:
		When it is constructing the tour data to be sent to the pda 
		1. if it finds a shippingpoint reference on the assignment part, then send that as point data together with it's id
		2. if it finds a shipto reference on the assignment part then depending on being lnf or not send the coordinates
		    stored on the assigment, or the ones from the shipto (the fix ones)
		
		The pda does not know if the id it received is a shipto or a shippingpoint id, but knows when to send that id back:
		if this id was paired with the unloading part (came from the 'wrapper of an unloading assignment part', 
		then it will send back the id when unloading, and so on for each assignment part.

		In the meantime Logon incoming mop handlers need to be adapted to handle the id received as described above correctly:
		in case of landfill interpret the received id in case of EnterShiptoRequest,DeliveryNoteRequest, LeaveShipToRequest
		as a shippingpoint id. 
		Fault message will still be: 30203 unknown ShiptoID in all the three cases as the field itself is named ShiptoID even if
		it carrier ShippingpointId.

		AsyncMopEventOutService.setRelevantBizeventPointId is the function which is called by all 3 of them to set the bizevent's
		shippingpoint id instead of shiptoId.

		 Cancelling on weigh system:
		    In case of landfill do NOT cancel the order if loaded via pda -> therefore guarantee that
		    the weighing system knows about the order. No further changes had been done, the message is the same
		    as normally, currently not clear if the weighing system will know that it's supposed to do the 
		    unloading and not the loading, and if it can handle that the time when it is supposed to to something
		    is not the planned loading time, but the planned unloading time.
		    THIS IS JUST THE FIRST STEP TAKEN ON BEHALF OF LANDFILL, FAR FROM COMPLETION.
		    CHANGED AT ALL YET.

		Persist&test: added landfill materials to lnf shipto's contract in order to be able to test how landfill
		    behaves with LNF. Assumption is that it will not work without further adaptation.

		Tested the followings:
		Admolo landfill order with an assignment where manually created drive-to part -> worked fine. 

		Question popped up: Silos needed to be specified, suppose this is because landfill is primarily specified as bulk, for now
		      supposed that leaving them empty and clicking continue without specifying anything is just fine?
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/eventbeans/in/mop/DeliveryNoteRequestHandler.java
