Created On    : 27-Jul-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5123
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2329, CUST180, ORDER1654, TERMINAL075: Cleanup postprocessing and validation of single delivery order creation
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   :   1. Structural change in constructing background data for determining available materials, and the valid settings for each of them:

		    Construction of objects which held these data: received a reference to a deliverysettingservice. Using the functions of this service to initialized themselves.
		    Problematic because it was complicated and also because entities were loaded in separate transactions -> there was
		    no chance to locate for example SapMaterialEntity of a shipto sarea restriction in the list of a loaded SapMaterialEntity.
		    Code solved this problem by using ListUtils.findListItemByPropertyValue and other util functions which simply locate
		    the material using PropertyUtils -> ok, but on the long run would be much better not to do that. First step to move
		    everything into a servicebean where entities can be compared much simpler.

		    Classes where the described change took place: DeliverySettingProductMap, DeliverySettingSalesAreaMap, DeliverySettingShiptoMap,
			DeliverySettingLanguageDependentResolver, GlobalTransportBackgroundData, MaterialAvailabilityBackgroundData, MaterialSelectionInitializer,
			 ShiptoSalesAreaFinancialbackgroundData

		  2. Changes on behalf of 1 resulted in a need for changeing validation and postprocessing
		    As validation and postprocessing regarding autoadd materials needed to initialize these structures, those are also affected by the
		    change even because their structure was also determined by the structure of the classes listed above: their construction was also
		    similar, received a parameter deliverySettingservice. They are also rewritten and moved to OrderServiceBean in the form of
		    postProcessOrder and validateOrder. 
		  
		    These functions are not yet final, and the screens using ValidationBeforeSave are not working yet - broken: call center, web order, pickup, handlers.

		    Restructured validation : structure of the saving action in web order and also call center: validate was separately called from the action.
			  The final goal is that saving orders has one single call to validateorder within orderservicebean, but in the meantime
			  if there are blocking validation errors the callers need to have human readable error messages, not proper to throw exception in
			  the validation. Currently it's throwing exception. As a next step ShiptoSalesAreaErrors will be reformed to resolve their messages 
			  automatically in order that we don't need those functions which were ment to load material descriptions, and other erroneous attributes.

		  3. Refactoring in bimodal order creation
		     Bimodal order creation was not easy to grasp the point because of bizevents coming and going around, started to refactor it at least to have
		      it in orderservice not in both order and bestellungservice.

		    Tests made before the commit: 
				bimodal order create -OK
				pickup not tested (already had blocker bug)
				call center ok
				web order ok
				fenics, wewas handers not tested

		   4. Also added initialization of order truck type list in case it was not set. On the long run the solution will be: checking the order's order
			  creation type code, and if at that place there was no chance to override, then take the vehicle list from the shipto/shipto sales
			  area default. Currently not considering this.
				  
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
