Created On    : 09-Aug-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5131
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2382, CUST182, COMMON657, ORDER1688: Validation messages are sent back to the actions
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Since ORDER1654 validation messages were not sent back to the actions, they simply threw LogonException,
		and therefore there was no chance to find out what the problem was. This was true to the request handlers.
		The setting if a certain validation error should cause failure or not was also not considered as 
		in case ther was an error it immediately threw exception.

		Introduced a new EJB ApplicationException which is currently supposed to roll back the transaction regardless of
		the flag shouldCauseFailure in ShiptoSalesAreaErrors.ERROR. For now this solution is OK as until now there are no such errors
		which are not supposed to cause failure on the order creation sources -> ok to to throw rollback exception.
		
		On order detail the update of the order is in a separate transaction, therefore the rollback exception
		will not roll back anything -> for now ok. On order detail  only quantity restriction is supposed to prevent saving
		this is made sure by checking what errors are amongst the detected problems, and an error will be shown and prevents
		starting the update transaction.

		ShiptoSalesAreaErrors.ERROR. shouldCauseFailure flag might need to be reviewed as they are
		like that completely ignored by the order creation sources! If someone would set something to false
		it would have no effect! Added a WARNING there into the code that it would not work as it is expected
		in the case of the order creation.

		In orderServicebean removed the unnecessary validateOrder and validateQuantities function as it was creating a
		list from a single order and then passed to the function which never gets other than one order since ORDER1654.
		It was there because of the bimodal order, when two orders were passed into these functions.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/eventbeans/in/logon_order_services/CreateOrderRequestHandler.java
