Created On    : 27-Aug-2012 / bartha
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2412, COMMON666, ORDER1702, PERSIST1853: Prototype for Plant_sarea - sarea->sorg - companycode authorization filtering 
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : 
The are special drop downs (i.e.: plant) where a large amount of data are present. Using the
hibernate entities to load the data is not possible as we might have over 10'000 objects (i.e.:100 sales areas, 100 plants = 10'000 objects, if plant_sarea is complete)).

Solution: Use DirectJpa with native SQL queries where "distinct" can be used on the needed columns --> we can keep the number of data low, as we select only the needed data.

Fix           : 
1.) DB: 
A new view is created to load the plant details by company code (VLGNC_PLANT_SAREA_COMPCODE):
tlgnr_plant_bs -> tlgnc_plant_sarea -> tlgnc_sarea -> tlgnr_sorg.COMPANYCODE_CD = *selection*

2.) BUSINESS: 
As this is a prototype, a new package is introduced (com.holcim.logon.business.services.directjpa). 
In the package are present the objects what are generating the native SQL Queries for the service beans.

These objects needs to impelmement two functions from the "NativeSQLData" interface:
"
	public String getNativeSQLQuery();
		
	public Object[] getQueryParams();
"

i.e. (Plant native SQL Query), 
getNativeSQLQuery() should return: 
"select distinct PLANT_CD, PLANT_NAME from VLGNC_PLANT_SAREA_COMPCODE where (1= 1) and COMPANYCODE_CD = ?2 
and (PLANT_CD is null or PLANT_CD IN (select PLANT_CD from TLGNU_USER_PLANT_ACC where USER_ID = ?1)) 
and (SAREA_ID is null or SAREA_ID IN (select SAREA_ID from TLGNU_USER_SAREA_ACC where USER_ID = ?1)) 
and (COMPANYCODE_CD is null or COMPANYCODE_CD IN (select COMPANYCODE_CD from TLGNU_USER_COMPANYCODE_ACC where USER_ID = ?1))"

NOTE: Also the user restriction MUST be present.

getQueryParams() should return:
[1241, 'AD01']

Important to always use similar 'directjpa objects', as we want to hide the implementation of script generation (easier to maintain)

Service Function (to load the plants):
PlantSareaServiceBean.java#getPlantList()

UI:
For the UI a new Helpper method is implemented (logon-common-web --> com.holcim.logon.web.utils#getPlantList()) --> returns a list of "com.holcim.logon.web.utils.DropdownEntity"
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
