Created On    : 27-Aug-2012 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-4621
ADN Change ID : PERSIST1854: order_numbers start at 20'000'000 in cluster 1
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : Holcim has issues with N clusters sending orders to the same SAP installation.
Description   : -
Fix           : Adjusting the order_number / custorder_number as follows:
		Cluster 0: 10000000 to 19999999 (-> see custom_sequences.sql, cluster 0 + if not overridden)
		Cluster 1: 20000000 to 29999999 -> see c1_initialdata
		Cluster 2: 30000000 to 39999999 -> c2_initialdata, once that folder/set of initialdata has been created, ca 2013
		Cluster 3: 40000000 to 49999999 -> c3_initialdata, once that folder/set of initialdata has been created, ca 2013/2014
		In AdN Environments, or in Holcim Q env, in cases where initialdata from more than 1 cluster is loaded
		=> last one wins. Adjust manually if NOK.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-persistence/etc/sql/custom_sequences.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/cl1_initialdata/initialdata_cl1.sql

