Created On    : 11-Sep-2012 / pascal
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5116
ADN Change ID : ORDER1744: Fixed Bug with automated order deletion
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : 
Fixed Bug with automated order deletion. If the quantity dropped to zero and there was no order left to be edited or deleted, the splitting also deleted orders, which are in a status beyond editing/deleting. This wrong behavior is fixed by this commit.
Correct behavior: the recalc tries to adjust/delete as long as orders are in a status, when they can be modified:

orderStatusCd.equals(Constant.ORDER_STATUS_NEW) ||
orderStatusCd.equals(Constant.ORDER_STATUS_TRANSMITTED_TO_POOL) ||
orderStatusCd.equals(Constant.ORDER_STATUS_TRANSMITTED_TO_POOL_ACK) ||
orderStatusCd.equals(Constant.ORDER_STATUS_TRANSMITTED_TO_CARRIER) ||
orderStatusCd.equals(Constant.ORDER_STATUS_TRANSMITTED_TO_CARRIER_ACK) ||
orderStatusCd.equals(Constant.ORDER_STATUS_DISPATCHED));

after these status, the splitting shall leave the orders, as they are, even if the ordering does deliver too much.
For the case, if there is the last delivery in an unchangable state and has exact quantity, a new sdo is created.. and so on.

Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/utils/CustorderUtils.java

