Created On    : 11-Sep-2012 / bartha
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : CFG266, COMMON681: 'HttpOnly' flag for the JSESSIONID cookie 
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : -
Fix           : 
				1.) Disable the filter by default
				2.) As at Login.jsp is the session created (also the JSESSIONID cookie generated), the filter-mapping#filter-name should be '/Login.jsp' (instead of "*.jsp")
				3.) The AJP Connector (check logon/container/conf/jboss-web.deployer/server.xml) 'emptySessionPath' attribute is set to 'true', check the attribute description:
				"
				If set to true, all paths for session cookies will be set to /. This can be useful for 
				portlet specification implementations, but will greatly affect performance if many 
				applications are accessed on a given server by the client. If not specified, this attribute is set to false.
				" 
				
				-->

				Use this path ("/") when overwriting the "SET-COOKIE" attribute (inside the filter). (NOTE: The server also sends this path)
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

