Created On    : 17-Sep-2012 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : PERSIST1899: cleanup of db creation / initialdata
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : Major cleanup of completely outdated initialdata from LOGON 1.x
		(che/nge), as well as better structure of
		a) Common (CL0 + CL1) and
		b) just FBNL (CL0) and
		c) just CHE/NGE/ITA (CL1)
		Major reason to do so:
		Holcim has decided to have all PLANTS, as well as all SALES AREAS
		from all clusters in all databases. Therefore, a too strict separation
		into countries simply does not make sense.
		I kept the files in their directories where we have input in seperate
		files (see tlngr_sorg.sql for now), but call them from 
		initialdata_2.1_all_clusters.sql.
Description   :
		Major reason for the restructuring:
		Holcim has decided to have all PLANTS, as well as all SALES AREAS
		from all clusters in all databases. Therefore, a too strict separation
		into countries simply does not make sense.
		I kept the files in their directories where we have input in seperate
		files (see tlngr_sorg.sql for now), but call them from 
		initialdata_2.1_all_clusters.sql.
		
		Reason for the deleation:
		If any of the old files would ever be needed, look
		for them in /share/install (or the archive). In reality, most of
		them would not even run anymore, because DB has changed so much
		since. Also, many tables have now "insert or update" scripts based
		on csv files. It's easier to copy those and reactivate old data,
		than to modify horribly old insert-sql sripts.
		I did leave a few of the old but 'main' scripts in the CVS, and
		mark with 'obsolete'. May help as an entry point to find old files.
Fix           : Fixed a few errors from fresh DB creation (last week,
		plus recent changes, e.g. in shipping condition) as well.
Workaround    : -
