Created On    : 21-Sep-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5298, LOGON-5394, LOGON-5421
ADN Change ID : COMMON698, BUSINESS2499,CUST191: Initialization of planned_unloading_time_min, transportation fields, unification of bimodal order creation
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Until now bimodal order creation called different single delivery order initialization function. In the meantime it turned out that
		even if there were if statements for rail orders, and it was supposed to handle all kind of deliveries, it was never called
		only for bimodal road order, a lot of code was there dealing with rail order -> risk is a little bit lower that the switch has
		a negative effect.

		From processSingleOrder cloning of the order was already removed sooner, from now on it will NOT clone the order, will NOT
		clone the order items, the only case if will clone one item is the special case of containers where there is an item multiplier
		which controls cloning of the order item, and adds it to the order.

		Did NOT check if bimodal rail item references are OK.
		Did NOT check if service items are added only once, though it is theoretically handled.

		From now allowing multiple bag items for the order in case the ordered uom is container -> this was prevented by the validation
		logic, and therefore prevented saving, though this is the basic case for the special container case.

		On the long run processSingleOrder is going to be removed completely, the necessary things should be moved to postprocessOrder method.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

