Created On    : 24-Sep-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5394
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2505, ORDER1779: Call hierarchy cleanup in customer order and order creation subject
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : CustorderServiceBean:
		  saveCustOrder_CustorderItems_Orders_OrderItems: commented out, it was basically doing the same as the current 
			  saveCustomerOrder: does the postprocessing for each single delivery orders
		  processOrdersOfCustorder: uncommented, no need for this function anymore, it was an iteration through the
			  sDOs and calling processSingleOrder -> that is explicitly in saveCustomerOrder
		  createCustomerOrder less parameter version -> 
			    1. visibbility reduced, it should only be accessed through the public createCustomerOrder
				function which requires the callers to specify if transmission to pool/carrier is required or not
			    2. renamed from create to processCustomerOrder as it is basically doing a type dependent split or simply
				initializing one single SDO
		  splitCustomerOrder: removed function, it's content is now explicit in the processCustomerOrder
		  createBimodalCustorder: the created sdos should be immediately transmitted to the commercial carrier

		  saveCustomerOrder public one: moved from BestellungService
		  persistCustomerOrder private one: moved from OrderService, it's purpose was either persist or merge the order after doing
			  a postprocessing step (init those fields which are not explicitly set by the order taking sources), nothing more
		
		BestellungServiceBean: commented out methods, they are moved mainly to CustorderServicebean
			    createArtifial... method moved to pickup servicebean as it is a pickup specific function and will only run for pickup
			    order

		OrderServiceBean:
			  saveCustomerOrder -> moved to CustorderServiceBean see above (persist&merge)
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
