Created On    : 26-Sep-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5458, LOGON-5404, LOGON-5451, LOGON-5467
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2531, ORDER1793, TERMINAL083: Customer order merging separated from customer order persist, pool/carrier/pickup handling
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : CustorderServiceBean:
 
		processCustomerOrder: it also did call saveCustomerOrder (=postprocess all SDOs and persist) but as persistCustomerOrder
			 does the automatic release to LDS for bulk orders it is not possible to do the persist before setting the statuses correctly
			 previously. Therefore this function does not call persist anymore explicitly, but just does the split(bulk)/clone(bag)
			 step and returns with the customer order togerhet with the orders. Note: the automatic release cannot be removed at this moment
			 from the persist as it is called from the call center as well, which already has the orders for the customer order.		

			 For bag after cloning there was a postProcessOrder and validateOrder, this step is already done in saveCustomerOrder, so it 
				  was there actually twice.
				      
		 createCustomerOrder:
		      1st step: call processCustomerOrder see above
		      2nd step: set the statuses explicitly according to the autopool autocarrier flags received
		      3rd step: 
		      Transmit to pool and transmit to carrier is not anymore explicitly called when
		      creating a customer order. It was not so before either, it complicates status handling, and also causes
		      failure for pickup bulk order creation.

		 former persistCustomerOrder: (postprocesscustorder then init order number and item number fields) handles persist and also merge

		 former saveCustomerOrder: This function was doing postprocessing and validation on the single delivery orders, and calling a former 
		      persistCustomerOrder (see above what that did).
		      As persistCustomerOrder was supposed to handle persist/merge too this method was called in case of
		      of merge (order detail = update customer order, pickup action = update customer order, endload = update customer order) and also
		      in case of persist (call center, web order/pickup/LDS (through createCustomerOrder)). As there are technical problems
		      anyway with merging the customer order (see LOGON-5451) apparently it's very risky to keep persist/merge together as 
		      what works for complete new customer order it does not always work for the merge.

		 persistCustomerOrder: contains all what saveCustomerOrder had + plus the parts of former persistCustomerOrder which were persist relevant

		 mergeCustomerOrder: contains postprocessing for the single delivery orders, but only in case the orders are new (i'm not sure that this
		      works properly, but tested with one click on customer order tab, it seemed to work, it might be that it only works because the split order
		      detail is doing is doing a clone, not creating an empty order, therefore not a problem if postProcessOrder has no initialization effect).

	      OrderServiceBean:
		  postProcessOrder: added checkOrderPrereq - this was responsible for initialization of the order validation code, and it was left out see LOGON-5404
  
		  endLoad: commented out triggering of split as it is still not working see technical problem LOGON-5451

		  postProcessOrder: in case of pickup set automatically pickup pool/carrier and set transmitted to carrier status (LOGON-5467)

	      PickupServiceBean: at the end of order creation from all sources there is a need to transmit to LDS (LOGON-5458) added this function. Reorganization 
		  is needed there too.
		
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/CustorderServiceBean.java
