Created On    : 03-Oct-2012 / bartha
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : ADMIN1009, BUSINESS2548, COMMON704: Update the JpaQueryData API + addapt the 'Assigned Carriers' new authorization in the User Admin 
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : -
Fix           : The Jpa Query generation API has been extended:
                An enum is introduced to store the colum names, and EnumSet are introduced for the select Query columns generation.
				The JpaQueryData will generate the select query columns based on the EnumSet. We can have more EnumSet for a JpaQueryData,
				this means we can perform diffrent select queries.
				JpaQueryData API:

				Whats new:
				1.) addSelectColumnNames(EnumSet<E> arg) :  Add an {@link EnumSet} with the column names to load. These columns will
				be generated into SQL select columns script.

				2.) getIndexOf(String columnName): Returns the index for the specified column from the SQL select query columns.
				If the column name was not specified for the select SQL query, <tt>-1</tt> is returned.
				where param columnName:
				      The name of the column whose index to get.


				+ User Admin: 'Assigned Carriers' adapt the new user authorization (LOGON-5295)
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
