Created On    : 06-Oct-2012 / bartha
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2580: Extend the JpaQueryData API with hasUserRestriction(Class<? extends BaseEntity> restrictionEntity) 
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : -
Fix           : A new function added for JpaQueryData hasUserRestriction(Class<? extends BaseEntity> restrictionEntity):

Return <code>true</code> if Jpa Query contains restriction for the given <code>restrictionEntity</code>,
	<code>false</code> otherwise. 
	This function can be called after getJpaQuery(), because the restriction are generated there. 
		@param
			restrictionEntity
				The restriction object to be checked.	
		@return
			Return <code>true</code> when the user has restriction, <code>false</code> otherwise


			Use this function at the user admin restriction assigment liast load.
