ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5582
ADN Change ID : TEST461: Tune Testdata to avoid confusion with real data
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : The test "Rail Standard Gauge" and the real CHE "Rail Standard Gauge"
		Pool were called identically. This is not just confusing to the user, but
		it could lead to problems if a component elimated duplicates.
		Not clear, if it causes things as observed in LOGON-5582
Description   : -
Fix           : Renamed the test pools to "ADZA..."
		What I want to avoid: Using the SAME pool for us (ADZA) and real world
		(CHE/Holcim). Reason: To date, I'm not aware that there is a hardcoding
		to exactly 1 standard narrow gauge pool (as is for pickup carrier/pool).
		It should be possible to have several, with the original meaning of
		"geographic splitting".
