Created On    : 12-Oct-2012 / nemes
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5451
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2635: Endload fails in case exact customer order quantity flag is on
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : The problem was quite interesting, so here it goes:
		  1) based on the customer order we create a new SDO, becaue this flag
		  2) this SDO is not persisted an added to the custorder's orders lazy collection
		  3) after the creation of the SDO it is not in a valif state (some not null attributes are null),
		      which will be set in a later stage in the workflow
		  4) we make several selects, and one of them triggers an autoflush
		  5) from the only one modified object (custorder) the autoflush cascades to all linked entities
		  6) because the actual state of the SDO is not correct the resulting (hibernate) EntityInsertAction 
		    creates a bogus SQL. The real interesting thing is that this event is an autoflush, so it creates
		    SQL, but it is not flushed to the DB (yet)
		  7) when the business logic actually issues the merge for the custorder, the SDO in question now
		    is a bogus INSERT + UPDATE to the latest state. The insert of course fails (null issue), but
		    it is very important to see that the insert was created way earlier (in 4-6)
Fix           : while traversing the critical codepath which does multiple selects, and updates the SDOs, detach the
		SDOs in question from the custorder, and after that manually persist them, and reattach to the custorder
		before issuing the merge in 7)
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/CustorderServiceBean.java
M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/OrderServiceBean.java

