Created On    : 17-Oct-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5298, LOGON-5642
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2675, TERMINAL090: All order taking sources call new bag split, pickup terminal changes
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : COMMIT AFFECTS LDS, WEB ORDER, PICKUP TERMINAL -> USING THE NEW BAG SPLIT

		AutoaddMaterialHelper changes probably were not worth to do because at the end it seems that
		autoadding will NOT be necessary for customer order level. Changed though in a manner that the returned
		object is a new OrderItemEntity instead of Autoadd material.

		DeliverySettingSalesAreaMap added helper method to be able to match a delivery setting based on restriction
		with a delivery setting which is basically the same but coming from the contract. (With this matching a
		customer order item which is created from a restriction and does not know anymore the restriction it was based on.

		DeliverySettingShiptoMap helper methods for retrieving only restriction based delivery settings.

		AbstractDeliverySetting: matching two delivery settings is now only according to the meaningful attributes, nothing
		else counts. In pickup this is necessary, at other places it is not even used.

		ValidateCustomerOrderRequestHandler: calling from now the same non-persisting version of customer order 'creation' what pickup
		      does, but the difference is that from postprocessOrder and postProcessCustorder removed sequence generation see LOGON-5642.
		      
		CreateOrderRequestHandler: anyway deprecated handler, but to use equivalent method as before: call finalInitOrder which initializes the
		      sequences as well.

		CustorderServiceBean - changed heavily, probably not final:
		    From CustOrderUtil moved here the retrieval of the valid vehicle type for the customer order.
		    Separated method which retrieves the vehicle type for the customer order from the actual customer order validation, but both need
		    currently the structure DeliverySettingSalesAreaMap to be able to find out the valid option configuration they need for the operation,
		    therefore it is passed in as parameter.
		    Since the vehicle types are now handled for bag as well, there is no need to have special conditions like only bulk, only road, only 
		    pikcup. The filter logic is supposed to be able to handle all kind of settings -> also removed if statements.
		
		    Created processCustomerOrder which can be called to handle the split, and also use the bag split, but at the end does NOT persist
		    the order, and does NOT do certain things like setting the sequence values. See LOGON-5462.

		    Removed parameter caller context, it is not needed anymore, the only context when the services are used is where no restrictions are
		    present, there is no need to pass the context in.

		    DeliverySettingServiceBean: Moved post filters from PickupOrderBean getRestrictionMapForShiptoSarea, as those have to be applied when loading
		    restrictions for the sales area structure (DeliverySettingSalesAreaMap).

		    OrderServiceBean: 
			Validation: ordered quantity = 0 is now allowed, as on the pickup terminal it was allowed for pallets.
			
			postProcessOrder method which is supposed to handle the autoadd feature: removed condition: except of pickup, as pickup also calls this function
			 in each round -> consequence: not possible to completely remove an autoadd material at the end if it was manually removed, it will be readded.
			  TODO clarify with Roland if this was a necessary thing. Option is to set the ordered quantity to 0.

		    PickupServiceBean: Removing assignment handling. From the Shipping screen it was also possible to merge the order items before calling load
			  otherwise the load would be incorrect -> as pickup reuses that function, which explicitly merges each order item (including the retured
			  quantity/uom which is the point on the pickup terminal for pallets) there is no need to handle this special case. In the old 1.6 system it was made sure
			  that in case loading happened from Logon and the loadOrderId was previously set -> it was automatically cancelled. Expect that this will also
			  work if the call comes from the pickup terminal.

			  setOrderLoaded: very similar to the one which works on Shipping screen (AuftragbearbeitungAction) difference is that here it's enough to copy the ordered 
			    quantity to loaded. Needs still cleanup.

		      Pickup overall: Conceptual change: the PickupOrderBean contains from now PickupPalletItems which belong to single delivery order items
			    and PickupCustomerOrderItemBean which basically belong to customer order item objects. The user can manage both on screen.

			    See limitation in LOGON-5298
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
