Created On    : 18-Oct-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2681, CUST198, TERMINAL092: Cleanup initialization of a new customer order
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Application behaviour is not supposed to changed, this is supposed to be an equivalent
		change.
		
		DONE:
		1. Dropped CustActionSupport it is good for nothing, completely empty.

		2. Added OrderTakingActionSupport which can use Actionsupport, Web order and pickup order
		already extend and use it.

		Later on probably will be moved to a service, or util, but at the moment it will do to have a common place
		for common initialization of objects in different Order taking screens (pickup, web order,
		call center).
		Already identified the common part which is common for pickup and web order, and added two
		functions named customInit this and that caller. Thus it's at one place instead of - currently
		- 2. On the long run it is supposed to hold also the call center immutable initialization,
		and if possible for LDS the same. 

		Also worth to consider to move certain parts to postprocess, or merge these functions with
		postprocessOrder in orderservicebean.

		The goal is to be able to see how fields are initialized according to CREATION_TYPE_CD,
		and DELIVERY_TYPE_CD, if they are different then see the differences at one place instead of
		having to look at 3-4 different places.

		3. Dropped not even used form fields from web order, they stuck there since 2009.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
