Created On    : 20-Oct-2012 / marius
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5036
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2724: 2.4 Order Detail Handling - Allowed Vehicle Types
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : The computation of order item numerator and denominator is now done
                by the new UomConverter service. Particular changes:
				* If the UOM of an order is Truck (LKW) or wagon, the net weight and/or
				  the volume of the trucks selected in the order or the wagon defined in
				  the shipto, respectively, are taken into account.
				* The truck or wagon with the highest priority is taken. If there are
				  several, the weight is used. If there are again several, the volume
				  is used for the comparison. 
				* Updated hibernate mappings so that a shipto's ShiptoTruckEntities and
			      ShiptoWagonEntities are eagerly fetched. 
				* Fixed the classpath for logon-business-client.jar to include the classes
			      in 'services/beans'. This to fix a build error caused by the new
				  UomConversionResult bean. 
				* Factored out vehicle comparison into dedicated, well-commented and unit-tested
				  methods in TruckWagonTypeWrapperUtil.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
