Created On    : 25-Oct-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-4877
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2761, CUST201, ORDER1866, TERMINAL096, PERSIST1985: Update of the customer order release functionality
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Refactored pickup transmission code to accept parameters from now on like the truck id, as that code is from now used for
		transmitting to the best match planning truck.

		Depending on the adjust times popup's autoRelease checkbox setting,  - which is now yet buggy, it needs to 
		click adjust deliveries button in order to take effect if unchecked - the orders will be transmitted to the
		best matching planning truck. The best matching planning truck determination reused the code which is used to update
		the ordered numerator/denominator's value. 

		The new assignment is transmitted to the planning truck, and all the steps will be done, which are normally done
		if someone releases on a planning truck - including releasing the freight cost calculation plan is also created.

		Probably will be asked to change later: the time to what the order is scheduled is the latest time until when the order
		needs to be loaded. This means that if everything goes according to this automatic plan there can be absolutely no
		being late for the order, but as this is only a plan, it might also be acceptable.

		For linking subcontractors updated the truck types for such values which currently seemed to be capable of
		carrying simple bag/bulk orders.

		From bimodal calls removed caller context, it was not used anymore.

		Validate and pickup order does not initialize the order statuses anymore, there is no need for that. That code part
		which uses the forwardToPool/forwardToCarrier/autoRelease flags is now at CustorderServiceBean.processNewOrders.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
