Created On    : 26-Oct-2012 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5722
ADN Change ID : PERSIST1987: moving blobs makes index of that table unusable. Call only in create DB.
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : ORA-01502: Index 'ULGN01.SYS_C00200428' oder Partition dieses Index in nicht brauchbarem Zustand
		select distinct(status), count(*) from user_indexes group by status;
		-> produces index in statue 'UNUSABLE'.
Description   : -
Fix           : Reason is: moving an attribute from 1 tablespace to another
		makes any index on that table invalid/UNUSABLE, unless the table
		(and therefore the index) is completely empty.
		That's why the problem was never found during db creation, and now only in db patching.
		solution:
		seperate 'move blob' from 'override index', and don't call each time
		during patching.
		Besides, fixed other (minor) errors during patching, such as obsolete
		net-price PL/SQL package, missing ; in custom_overrides.sql, etc.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

A logon-persistence/etc/sql/custom_create_move_blobs.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/custom_overrides.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/objs.sql
M logon-persistence/etc/sql/patch/from_2.1.0.3/patch_above_2.1.0.3.sql

