Created On    : 26-Oct-2012 / uma
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : PERSIST1989: Provide a containe for "patches" of test/adnovum-initialdata
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : During the last week we found an issue regaring updates of RELEVANT
		adnovum-invented testdata/initialdata. E.G., a new feature will require
		updating testdata in a suitable way, so that it is testable in-house.
		- In a DEV environment, all of these statements are simply executed immediately
		- For a FRESH db, they will be executed together with the create scripts
		- BUT: for a DB such as TLGNEBM1, used for integration tests, there is a
		  gap, because that DB is updated only LATER, with PATCH scripts, and
		  it is cumbersome to update the testdata accordingly as well.
		- It would be WRONG to add these updates to the patch script, because
		  the patch is STRICTLY HOLCIM ONLY, and shall not be optimized for any
		  of our AdNovum-internal dev/test issues.
		- It would be WRONG to simply execute all "insert" scripts again: there would
		  be lots of (bogus) errors, and if a record already exists, it won't be
		  updated.... 
Description   : -
Fix           : Please collect all your updates to initial/test data which are
		ADNOVUM ONLY, i.e. belonging to ADZA, in this newly created file.
		+ add to the initialdata/testdata scripts as before.
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

A logon-persistence/etc/sql/patch/from_2.1.0.4/update_adnovum_initial_and_testdata.sql

