Created On    : 28-Oct-2012 / marius
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5660
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2776: Bimodal order creation failure
Symptoms      : Getting a suitable truck would fail sometimes with an exception.
Description   : The behavior of the old code of TruckWagonTypeWrapperUtil.findProperTruck()
                was that if an empty list was passed as input then null was returned.
				In our change to implement findProperTruck() as a combination of compareTo()
				and Collections.max(), I omitted a check for an empty list. Collections.max()
				throws a NoSuchElementException if the input list is empty.
Fix           : The function findProperTruck() now first checks for an empty list and returns
                an explicit null in that case.
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/utils/TruckWagonTypeWrapperUtil.java
