---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Created On    : 30-Oct-2012 / marius
ADN Bugzilla  : -
ADN Change ID : COMMON756: Made name and value of DropdownEntity class immutable
Description   : Small DTO classes like this should be made immutable whenever possible.
                The pattern of
				<code>
				MyClass a = new MyClass();
				a.setName("xyz");
				a.setValue("abc");
				</code>
				is very ugly and doesn't enforce any invariants about the class.
				When encountering an object of type MyClass you never know if its fields
				have been initialized or not, and are forced to do tedious null checks
				(and in many cases don't even know what to do if a field is unexpectedly
				null). 
				See also the mail from romek to logon-dev with subject
				"Services/methods with multiple return values".
Fix           : Made the 'name' and 'value' fields of DropdownEntity final, removed the
                default constructor, and updated the code wherever an instance was created.
				Note that all occurrences of the default constructor were followed by 
				calls to setName() and setValue(), exactly the "bad" pattern shown above.
Affected Files:

M logon-common-web/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/web/utils/CheckboxDropdownEntity.java
M logon-common-web/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/web/utils/DropdownEntity.java
