Created On    : 31-Oct-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5671, LOGON-5729, LOGON-5572
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2803, COMMON761, ORDER1889, TERMINAL097: Introduced various validation reasons, different and yet the same validation for merge/persist order
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Similarity of add service handler and order detail: they both add services, and they both need the same initialization for the new 
		order items, what is present in create custorder/order. To complicate the situation even more on order detail there is no such that the order
		is validated separately from the order items, and validation errors for not new order items should only be sent back to the user as warning = does not
		block saving. Besides certain errors should under all circumstances block saving like the quantity restriction check failure, and customer order
		block, this is true for already existing orders as well.

		Therefore introduced ValidationErrorReason class which contains all the information needed to be able to determine the correct reaction to the
		validation errors. If the validation error happens with a new item -> all should block. If the validation error happens with an already existing item
		-> do not block. 

		On order detail if ValidationException is thrown that will roll back. For the moment reused the already existing strange map structure to send back
		the validation errors in case there are. Validation is in a separate transaction to guarantee that it will never roll back the saving in case
		the caught exception is not thrown further (like in case of new order item validation and quantity restriction&blocking errors).

		ValidationErrorReason has multiple subclasses, all of them tried to reflect what exactly they are supposed to repesent: an error on order level,
		order item level, customer order item level, customer order level, or even integrity error like bag + bulk cannot appear, etc. 
      
		The current existing validation errors are present in CustorderError class.

		For reusing initialization of new order items faced the same problem than in BUSINESS2635, see description there, currently the solutio
		is the same as there, added a lot of javadoc what exactly we're trying to work around there. Here it is in OrderServiceBean detachNewOrderItems.

		For services if production plant is left empty from the order taking screens/callers the production plant will be determined for the first material
		item. See LOGON-5272.

		Removed actually not validation but implementation exceptions like NO_CUSTORDER_FOR_ITEM and such. There was no point to define caller dependent message
		for them, the user actually cannot really do anything against them.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/build.xml
M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/ordercreation/InvalidMapSupport.java
