Created On    : 09-Nov-2012 / emoke
ADN Bugzilla  : LOGON-5572
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2869: AddService handler: adjusting quantities depending on the order status
Cust Bug ID   : -
Platform      : -
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Add service handler has to add the specified quantity in case it turns out that
		the order is above loaded status.

		Added general function to OrderService which receives the necessary parameters
		to be able to decide if the operation is permitted or not, and to be able to to adapt the quantities
		as follows:
	    
		below status loaded: add the specified quantity to the ordered quantity if material specified, uom specified corresponds with the order item ordered uom
		above loaded: add the specified quantity to the delivered quantity if material specified, uom specified corresponds with the order item delivered uom

		Conversion is not supported here, as currently this function is only used for services, where conversion is not much supposed
		to be used. If the function later on is used for materials then conversion needs to be added.

		Only services are allowed to be changed after loaded. Before loaded there is no check regarding anything as below loading
		the operation does not need to include changes on load.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Release Notes : -
Dependants    : -
Requires      : -
Pkg Changes   : -
