Created On    : 16-Nov-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-5396
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2922: Delivery Note Generation Fails with ArithmeticException
Symptoms      : An ArithmeticException (msg: "Non-terminating decimal expansion;
				no exact representable decimal result.") occurred when creating a
				delivery note for a cash sales order.
Description   : The division involved in the computation of net value and vat value
				did not specify scale or rounding mode. The result of the division
				involved could therefore not be represented as a decimal fraction with
				finite precision.
Fix           : Introduced constants MONEY_SCALE and MONEY_ROUNDING_MODE in
				Constants.java (to centralize the definition of rounding precision and
				mode), and explicitly specifying these for the divisions in question.
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/OrderServiceBean.java
M logon-common/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/constants/Constant.java

Test Ref      : -
Documentation : -
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Created On    : 16-Nov-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-5936
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS2923: Delivery Note Generation Fails with ArithmeticException
Symptoms      : The printed amount on the cash sales delivery note 
				was 6699.90 or something like that even though the net value
				in the contract was 6700 and the ordered quantity was equal to the
				target quantity of the contract.
Description   : The code first divided the net value by the target quantity and then
				multiplied by the ordered quantity. Because of the rounding
				introduced in BUSINESS2922, some precision was lost, leading to
				6700 / 30 * 30 = 6699.90.
Fix           : First multiplying then dividing -> no loss of precision. 
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/OrderServiceBean.java

