Created On    : 22-Nov-2012 / emoke
ADN Ticket ID : -
ADN Change ID : SIMUL113, CFG292: Attempt to ease url setting for NB and also for dev testing
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Problem 1: if someone changes the url of any of the test requests to a different url
		    than localhost -> test would fail for others, who want to use localhost, and who does not spot this fact.

		Problem 2: from the xml file it's out of question that anyone spots that he/she is going to commit the url change, because
		    lines are tousends of characters long

		Problem 3 (nightly build): Soapui and logon is not on the same machine localhost is not ok, but
		    sometimes the paths also differ for the NB and another instance, there is a need to be able to 
		    control the urls better.

		What I tried to do is the following:

		1. Added 2 more project properties, see the purpose at 2: ldstologonportpath & mopeventportpath

		2. Set centrally on the MockEventPort settings the endpoint to ${#Project#testhosturl}${#Project#ldstologonportpath}
		    which is set from testhosturl and ldstologonportpath from the project properties.

		    Set centrally on the LDSToLogonPort settings the endpoint to ${#Project#testhosturl}${#Project#mopeventportpath}
		    which is set from testhosturl and mopeventportpath from the project properties.

		    (available on the UI: right click on integration-tests and click 'Show project view', access 'Properties'
		    tab -> there you can see the default testhosturl ldstologonportpath and mopeventportpath. 
		    
		    The url therefore  where LDS sends the messages is: testhosturl concatenated with ldstologonportpath
		    The url therefore  where LDS sends the messages is: testhosturl concatenated with mopeventportpath
		
		Until everyone keeps it that way, and does not change the endpoint to something else, and commits the integration xml file
		this will make sure that everyone can use soapui and will nto be blocked by problems due to this.

		Intermediate description of the problem in the NB: 
		     CEM test suite would have failed because it would wrongly send the mop message to the lds endpoint. This is a big problem
		     as the NB tests were designed to use ONE single endpoint specified in the build-test.xml targeturl, and therefore
		     this endpoint was specified for all calls, including now the mop requests, which is simply wrong. We need 2 urls and in a 
		     parametrized manner: 1 for lds and 1 for the mop.

		  3. There is 3 possibilities to call test-int-macro: 

		      Possibility 1: specify endpoint url - AS WAS

		      as until now calling with parameter targeturl (but renamed it to endpoint, as that
		      describes for what that url is actually used: testrunner.sh parameter -e means: endpoint, the url where ALL the requests will be sent.
		      All tests are calling test-int-macro with this parameter (as until now), but 'CEM Test Suite', that is using the possibility 2.

		    
		      Possibility 2: specify testhosturl, mopeventportpath and ldstologonportpath one by one for test-int-macro ant macro- NEW
		      -> until no one changes the ${#Project#testhosturl}${#Project#ldstologonportpath} endpoint it is fine.

		      Possibility 3: not specifying anything when calling test-int-macro
		      This will make sure that if someone for some reason changed the urls to different ones, then the target does not 
		      override the setting. 

		    Best would be that NB can declare that the endpoint has to come from ${#Project#testhosturl}${#Project#ldstologonportpath}, but fo
		    the moment I'm not aware how that can be done.

		   Removed WorfklowTest, that is replaced by CEM Test Suite.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M config/build-dev.properties
M config/build-nightly.properties
M logon-simulator/build-test.xml
M logon-simulator/etc/soapui/integration-tests/integration-tests-soapui-project.xml
M logon-simulator/etc/soapui/manual-tests/manual-tests-soapui-project.xml

