Created On    : 26-Nov-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6032
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3022: Make struts actions more resilient to direct calls
Component     : -
Symptoms      : Calling an Action's URL directly (instead of the corresponding
				EntryAction's) leads to errors (especially in the log).
Description   : When the Action/EntryAction paradigm is used, the action's execute()
				often assumes that the required data has been loaded into the
				respective Struts form by the EntryAction. If this assumption is not
				true, NullPointerExceptions are often the result.
				While not technically a bug, the exceptions still pollute the log.
Fix           : A more robust solution is a check at the beginning of the Action; 
				if any required data has not yet been loaded, redirect to the entry action.
Affected Files:

M logon-admin-web/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/admin/web/actions/truckadmin/TruckAdminAction.java
M logon-order-web/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/order/web/actions/raildispo/DispoAction.java
M logon-order-web/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/order/web/actions/simpledispo/SimpleDispoAction.java

