Created On    : 06-Dec-2012 / emoke
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6125
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3107: Do not try to restore planned delivery times in case there was no pre-planning
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : Operations which can trigger moveAssignment since LOGON-5935:
		    deallocate from real truck
		    moveAssignment explicitly called by LDS or scheduling UI

		Deallocate from real truck: in this case the assignment is going to be set to status 
		    released_by_prescheduler  and the values stored in pre_planned_start is going to be set to 
		    the planned_start fields. This was the intention of the erroneous code part.

		The problem described in the ticket is that in case there was no pre-planning
		the planning_truck field is null, and there is no planning data at all -> restoring non-existent
		planning data messes up the assignment.

		Added check to setPreplannedData function: if the assignment holds no planning_truck_id information
		there was no release on a planning truck ever -> do not try to restore the timing data, but go on
		as normally if moving an assignment from one truck to another.
Fix           : -
Workaround    : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/OrderServiceBean.java

