Created On    : 11-Dec-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6133
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3119: Fixed creation of performance orders with service materials
Symptoms      : When attempting to create a performance order with an additional
				service material, an error message occurred "only one of the parameters
				should be defined at performance orders ('delivery to date' or
				'ordered quantity')".
Description   : There was a check for performance orders that if a delivery qty/frequency
				is set, then no order item must have an ordered quantity set. This check
				was wrong for service items, since they can still have an ordered quantity
				(e.g. 1 PCE) even if the material item has a frequency specified.

				As a follow up problem, it turned out that the UOM was not determined
				properly for the material item if a service item was added. The original code
				tried to take the UOM entity for the material item from the list of loaded
				UOMs for the dropdown. However, this list contained the UOMs for the
				service item if any service item was added. As a fix, the UOM entity is now
				loaded directly from the refdata service.
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/utils/CustorderUtils.java
M logon-order-web/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/order/web/actions/bestellung/BestellungAction.java

