Created On    : 11-Dec-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6155
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3123: Gracefully handling empty transport pools
Symptoms      : In the production environment at Holcim, a fatal error occurred
				when one tried to open a shipto in the order entry screen (call
				center).
Description   : The reason was that in that environment, no rail pools existed.
				The code in PoolAdminService.fetchPoolTxEntitiesByDeliveryType()
				caused an IllegalArgumentException in Restrictions.in() if no
				pools of the specified transport type existed in the DB.
Fix           : If there are no pools of a specified type, the method now simply
				returns an empty list.
Workaround    : Install a single dummy rail pool (as done by stich in production,
				see ticket).
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/PoolAdminServiceBean.java

Test Ref      : Tested on DLGNHU02 by temporarily changing the transport type
				of all rail pools to road pools.
