Created On    : 14-Dec-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6183
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3143: Removing pre-planning data when merging assignments
Symptoms      : Weird assignment states could occur if pre-planned orders were merged
				on a real truck, depending on the order in which the merging was done.
Description   : It does not make sense to keep pre-planning data in an assignment with
				several orders that were independently planned. The merged assignment
				would contain the planning truck ID of only one of the orders, but
				the planned times for both. 
Fix           : When two assignments are merged, the planning truck ID and the pre-planned-start
				times are set to (null).

				Note that if the user merges two pre-planned assignments "by accident", then
				the pre-planning data is therefore irreversibly lost. This is mitigated, however,
				by the fact that the merging already triggers a cancel notification to LDS, which
				is also irreversible.
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/OrderServiceBean.java

Test Ref      : -
Documentation : -
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Created On    : 14-Dec-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6139
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3144: Correctly handling remote UOM exceptions
Description   : There was a catch for LogonConversionException in the web tier, which
				would convert the exceptions into warning messages. However, since these
				are runtime exceptions, they are packaged into an EJBException and "escaped"
				the catch clause.
Fix           : Catching EJBException and checking if the cause is instanceof LogonConversionException.
				Better fix for future: Change exception type to checked; checked exceptions are
				thrown as is by EJB standard and not packaged in EJBExceptions. But this will require
				some changes to our EJB GDI generator...
Affected Files:

M logon-order-web/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/order/web/actions/OrderActionSupport.java
