Created On    : 19-Dec-2012 / paksyd
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-5221
ADN Change ID : DISPO529: Could not calculate route status=ZERO RESULTS
Component     : -
Symptoms      : In some cases the Truck route could not be displayed on a popup map and a 
				warning message was shown "Could not calculate route status=ZERO RESULTS" 
				because the Google Map API returned no route data and status ZERO_RESULTS.
Description   : -
Fix           : For route calculation the caller can define waypoints to include in the route. 
				The waypoint has an optional attribute "stopover", which is set to false in LOGON, 
				but the default value is true.

				According to the documentation:
				https://developers.google.com/maps/documentation/javascript/directions#Waypoints

				"stopover (optional) indicates whether this waypoint is a actual stop on the route (true) or
				instead only a preference to route through the indicated location (false). 
				Stopovers are true by default."

				There is no clue why the waypoints are not considered as actual stops on the route.

				Investigation showed, if we change "stopover:false" to the default (stopover:true), 
				those cases which resulted "ZERO RESULTS" before, are working fine.

				Therefore from now on we use stopover:true to all waypoints on the Truck scheduling screen and 
				in the assignment edit popup.
Workaround    : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-order-web/src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/jsp/dispo/DispoTile2.jsp
M logon-order-web/src/main/webapp/js/editAssignment.js

