Created On    : 19-Dec-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6165
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3154: Don't return same auto-add material twice
Component     : Call center order taking screen
Symptoms      : An error occurred if a pickup order was created with two bag materials,
				for both of which the same auto-add material was configured.
Description   : The code that adds the order items for the auto-add materials
				correctly checks if there is an existing order item with the
				auto-add material type, and if so, just updates that item's quantity.
				However, in such a case the method AutoaddMaterialHelper.createAutoAddMaterial()
				should have returned null, to indicate that no new item must be
				added to the order's item list.

				Wrongly, it did not return null, but returned the updated item
				again. As a result, the item of the auto-add material was contained
				twice in the order item list. This lead to confusion when creating the
				assignments and load (which is done automatically because it is a
				pickup order).

				In other cases (no pickup, no autorelease), this doesn't cause any trouble,
				because once the list of order items is persisted and later reloaded,
				then the reloaded list will no longer contain the duplicate item
				(because on the DB there is only one item).
Fix           : AutoaddMaterialHelper.createAutoAddMaterial() returns null if it updated
				an existing order item.
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/ordercreation/AutoaddMaterialHelper.java
M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/OrderServiceBean.java

