Created On    : 20-Dec-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6020
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3158,PERSIST2135: Manually combining simple vehicle load items and loading points
Component     : Simple vehicle scheduling
Symptoms      : Some errors occur during DB patching (in particular index creation), because the generated
				code attempted to create indices and foreign key constraints for views.
Description   : To understand why this happened, some background is necessary. The data in question is used
				to populate the "load" popup of the simple vehicle scheduling screen. There, all loadable
				order items are listed, and each order item has a dropdown with the possible loading points.

				Thus, the order items and loading points are in a 1:N relation to each other. They are
				provided by the two views VLGNC_SIMPVEH_LOAD_ORDER_ITEM and VLGNC_SIMPVEH_LOADINGPOINT,
				respectively.
				
				When I implemented the business service for the loading popup, I thought it would be
				possible to declare (in the XML entity definition of VLGNC_SIMPVEH_LOADINGPOINT and
				in mappings.properties) a foreign key constraint/OneToMany relationship, such that 
				hibernate automatically loads the items from VLGNC_SIMPVEH_LOADINGPOINT for each
				row of VLGNC_SIMPVEH_LOAD_ORDER_ITEM.

				This worked in the implementation, but gdi-jpa also generated foreign key definitions
				and indices for the view in the generated DDL files. While not doing any damage, this
				led to the observed errors each time the DB was patched.

				In the interest of simplicity, I have decided to revert to a simpler implementation,
				where I separately load the matching rows from each of the two views, and then combine them
				manually, just like it was alread done by SimpleVehicleSchedulingService.getUnallocatedOrders().
Affected Files:

A logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/beans/SimpleVehicleLoadableItem.java
