Created On    : 21-Dec-2012 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6182
ADN Change ID : COMMON805: Support for checked exceptions in EJB Business Delegates/Dispatchers
Description   : Added proper support for checked exceptions in the gdi-generated EJB
				Business Delegates and Dispatchers.
				Any exception declared in the throws clause of a public EJB method can
				now be caught in a try/catch block by the EJB client as is.

				That is, while previously you had to do something convoluted like this:
				<code>
				catch (EJBException e) {
					Throwable cause = e.getCause();
					
					if (!(cause instanceof LogonConversionException)
							|| !((LogonConversionException) cause).isReason(Reason.RES_ERROR_UOM_CONV_FUZZY_UOM)) {
						throw e;
					}
					else {
						// handle the LogonConversionException here
					}
				}
				</code>
				now you can do this much more easily as
				<code>
				catch (LogonConversionException e)
				{
					// handle the LogonConversionException here
				}
Affected Files:

M logon-business/etc/gdi/ejb3/templates/BusinessDelegate.java.vm
M logon-business/etc/gdi/ejb3/templates/Dispatcher.java.vm
M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/UomConverterServiceBean.java
