Created On    : 03-Jan-2013 / paksyd
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-5635 
ADN Change ID : DISPO530: Scheduling screen: dragging bars used to show more or less Planning trucks, Real trucks and Orders
Component     : -
Symptoms      : When the user dragged the resize bar between planning trucks and real trucks 
				the sections were not precisely resized according to the dragging distance.
Description   : Problem:
				The code which calculated the new proportions of the planning and real trucks 
				section always subtracted 40 pixel from the dragging bar vertical coordinate.
				This resulted the above described awkward behaviour.

				Background:
				On the original scheduling screen only one dragging bar existed between the 
				Scheduling (trucks) and the Orders section.
				The top of the Orders section contained a row with the section title and links 
				("Return order finished", "Unloaded", etc.). The dragging bar was located 
				between this row and the orders table. 
				For this reason the proportion calculating logic should subtract 40 pixel from 
				the dragging bar vertical coordinate to compensate this extra row above the 
				dragging bar.
				The new dragging bar (between planning and real trucks) implementation based on 
				this one also adopted this subtract 40 pixels rule, but there is no reason to 
				leave it that way, because no extra row exists.
Fix           : Without the 40 pixel substraction from the dragging bar vertical coordinate 
				the dragging distance considered well, resulting the sections are precisely 
				resized according to the dragging distance.
Workaround    : -
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-order-web/src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/jsp/dispo/DispoTile2.jsp

