Created On    : 03-Jan-2013 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6231
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3165: Skipping load takeover quantity check for fuzzy UOMs
Component     : Truck scheduling screen
Symptoms      : An order with ordered quantity "1 LKW" could not takeover a truck load
				of "27.38 tons".
Description   : The code in OrderService.checkLoadTakeover() did a check so that a load
				can only be taken over if it's not more than 105% of the ordered quantity.
				However, if the ordered UOM was fuzzy (such as LKW), it would not consider
				the load for takeover.
				From a business perspective, this is wrong. It should always be possible to take
				over a load if the order has a fuzzy UOM.
Fix           : Skipping the quantity check for fuzzy ordered UOMs. I.e., a load with matching
				material and production plant can always be taken over for a fuzzy order,
				regardless of the quantity.
Workaround    : Change the order's UOM to a nonfuzzy one such as TONS. 
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/OrderServiceBean.java

