Created On    : 18-Jan-2013 / paksyd
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6203, LOGON-6220
ADN Change ID : DISPO535: Fix for inresponsive dragging and duplication of delivery boxes
Component     : -
Symptoms      : If there is two deliveries belonging to an exact customer order, 
				scheduled (but not released) to different trucks the following issue appears:
				If the planning section is hidden and the assignment is close to the bottom edge 
				of the visible area, and if you try to move the assignment horizontally 
				the assignment jumps back to it's original position. 
				This lefts the screen in an inconsistent state.
				After dragging the upper assignment results duplication of the lower one till 
				the next screen refresh.
Description   : The code calculates the top of the dispo section based on the top of the 
				*planning section*.
				If the planning section is *hidden*, the top of it will be *zero*.
				The wrongly calculated top variable is used to calculate the bottom of the 
				dispo section as well.
				This leads to that it is not possible to move assignment horizontally.
Fix           : If the planning section is hidden use the real one, if the real section is 
				hidden, use the planning one to calculate the top value.
				(Also removed the TODO from marius which marked this code to check.)
Workaround    : Possible workaround would be to scroll the truck list so the assignment 
				would be upper from the bottom edge of the visible area.
Pkg Changes   : -
Affected Files:

M logon-order-web/src/main/webapp/js/dispo2.js

