Created On    : 29-Jan-2013 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6392
ADN Change ID : BUSINESS3217: Comment and verbose error message for errors in rail tariff selection
Component     : Rail scheduling
Symptoms      : Rail order could not be transmitted to SBB
Description   : The error was due to bad data in tlgnc_rail_tariff. Logon tries to find
				a matching tariff for the order/wagon by successively applying looser
				criteria until it finds a match. However, these criteria are never supposed
				to lead to more than 1 results, otherwise the code failed with a
				NonUniqueResultException, which is exactly what happend in the incident
				for which this ticket was opened.
				I have now put the DB query inside a catch clause, and if a
				NonUniqueResultException is thrown, a verbose error message is logged,
				indicating that it is probably a data error.
Affected Files:

M logon-business/src/main/java/com/holcim/logon/business/services/impl/EdifactImportServiceBean.java

