Created On    : 04-Feb-2013 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6296
ADN Change ID : DISPO544: Prevent parallel refreshes of same objects in dispo screen
Component     : Truck scheduling screen
Description   : If the systems are under extreme load, it is conceivable that the auto
				refresh scheduler task starts a new update request even if the previous
				is still pending.
				The implementation uses a refresher object with a state in a closure;
				the state has a variable refreshInProgress, which is set to true
				until the callback has completed.
				See makeRefresher() which produces a refresher object, and the
				truckRefresher and orderRefresher objects for an example how it's used.

				As a tool, I've also added a dispoDebug() function. This function does nothing
				by default, but if you set (e.g. in Firebug or in the webconsole) the variable
				dispoDebugEnabled to true, then you can see debug messages.

				The refresher object uses dispoDebug().

				To test, do the following in the console:
					dispoDebugEnabled = true;
					updateTask.interval = 500;  // very small update interval to simulate parallel updates
Affected Files:

M logon-order-web/src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/jsp/dispo/DispoTile2.jsp

