Created On    : 04-Feb-2013 / marius
ADN Ticket ID : LOGON-6296
ADN Change ID : DISPO545: Minimum time before refreshing
Component     : -
Symptoms      : -
Description   : To improve performance of the scheduling screen, I added a new
				config parameter app.default.dispo.min.time.before.reload.
				If less than this number of seconds has elapsed before the last
				refresh of trucks or orders has elapsed, then the next refresh
				is skipped.
				This is to give the user a minimal time to work.
				The default value is set to 60 seconds.
				The default refresh interval is set to 120 seconds. So if a
				refresh takes (in an extreme case) 100 seconds, then the next refresh
				won't take place, because 20 s < 60 s.
				This can also be set to 0 (or something negative) to disable 
				the feature.
Affected Files:

M logon-order-web/src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/jsp/dispo/DispoTile2.jsp
M logon-persistence/etc/csv/refdata/config.csv

